        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The surface called \"surface\" means the lower boundary of the atmosphere. \"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area. \"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Ra\" means the element \"radium\" and \"228Ra\" is the isotope \"radium-228\" with a half-life of 2.45e+03 days."@en;
