        skos:definition        "The surface called \"surface\" means the lower boundary of the atmosphere. \"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area. \"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Xe\" means the element \"xenon\" and \"131mXe\" is the metastable state of the isotope \"xenon-131\" with a half-life of 1.18e+01 days."@en;
