        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "\"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Radioactivity concentration\" means radioactivity per unit volume of the medium. \"Cd\" means the element \"cadmium\" and \"111mCd\" is the metastable state of the isotope \"cadmium-111\" with a half-life of 3.39e-02 days."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::Z8C3JGXG";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "radioactivity_concentration_of_111mCd_in_air"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/BQM3/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/RK9C1CMU/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::RK9C1CMU";
        dc:date                "2018-10-15 12:56:49.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::RK9C1CMU";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-10-15 12:56:49.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/RK9C1CMU/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/sea_surface_wave_mean_square_x_slope/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/sea_surface_wave_mean_square_x_slope>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "Wave slope describes an aspect of sea surface wave geometry related to sea surface roughness. Mean square slope describes a derivation over multiple waves within a sea-state, for example calculated from moments of the wave directional spectrum. The phrase \"x_slope\" indicates that slope values are derived from vector components along the grid x-axis."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::RK9C1CMU";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "sea_surface_wave_mean_square_x_slope"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/UUUU/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/09VD5LSX/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::09VD5LSX";
        dc:date                "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::09VD5LSX";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/09VD5LSX/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_148Pm_in_air/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_148Pm_in_air>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The phrase \"integral_wrt_X_of_Y\" means int Y dX. The data variable should have an axis for X specifying the limits of the integral as bounds. The phrase \"wrt\" means \"with respect to\". \"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Radioactivity concentration\" means radioactivity per unit volume of the medium. \"Pm\" means the element \"promethium\" and \"148Pm\" is the isotope \"promethium-148\" with a half-life of 5.38e+00 days."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::09VD5LSX";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_148Pm_in_air"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/BSM3/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/95SAHUOK/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::95SAHUOK";
        dc:date                "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::95SAHUOK";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/95SAHUOK/1/>;
