        skos:definition        "Mole fraction is used in the construction mole_fraction_of_X_in_Y, where X is a material constituent of Y.   The chemical formula of  nitrous oxide is N2O."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CFV8N44";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "mole_fraction_of_nitrous_oxide_in_air"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/UUUU/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV11N8/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CFV11N8";
        dc:date                "2017-11-28 06:51:06.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CFV11N8";
        pav:authoredOn         "2017-11-28 06:51:06.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV11N8/2/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV11N8/1/>;
        pav:version            "2";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "true";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/VL5QBNPI/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/integral_of_surface_downwelling_longwave_flux_in_air_wrt_time> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/integral_of_surface_downwelling_longwave_flux_in_air_wrt_time/>;
        owl:versionInfo        "2";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P64/current/G210/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P64/current/G206/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P02/current/LWRD/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P04/current/G206/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P04/current/G210/>;
        skos:definition        "\"integral_of_Y_wrt_X\" means int Y dX. The data variable should have an axis for X specifying the limits of the integral as bounds. \"wrt\" means with respect to. The surface called \"surface\" means the lower boundary of the atmosphere. \"longwave\" means longwave radiation. Downwelling radiation is radiation from above. It does not mean \"net downward\". When thought of as being incident on a surface, a radiative flux is sometimes called \"irradiance\". In addition, it is identical with the quantity measured by a cosine-collector light-meter and sometimes called \"vector irradiance\". In accordance with common usage in geophysical disciplines, \"flux\" implies per unit area, called \"flux density\" in physics."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CFV11N8";
        skos:note              "deprecated"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "integral_of_surface_downwelling_longwave_flux_in_air_wrt_time"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/WSMM/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/VL5QBNPI/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::VL5QBNPI";
        dc:date                "2018-07-03 16:09:23.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::VL5QBNPI";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-07-03 16:09:23.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/VL5QBNPI/2/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/VL5QBNPI/1/>;
        pav:version            "2";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV11N8/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/integral_wrt_time_of_surface_downwelling_longwave_flux_in_air/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/integral_wrt_time_of_surface_downwelling_longwave_flux_in_air>;
        owl:versionInfo        "2";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The phrase \"integral_wrt_X_of_Y\" means int Y dX. The data variable should have an axis for X specifying the limits of the integral as bounds. The phrase \"wrt\" means with respect to. The surface called \"surface\" means the lower boundary of the atmosphere. Downwelling radiation is radiation from above. It does not mean \"net downward\". The sign convention is that \"upwelling\" is positive upwards and \"downwelling\" is positive downwards. The term \"longwave\" means longwave radiation. When thought of as being incident on a surface, a radiative flux is sometimes called \"irradiance\". In addition, it is identical with the quantity measured by a cosine-collector light-meter and sometimes called \"vector irradiance\". In accordance with common usage in geophysical disciplines, \"flux\" implies per unit area, called \"flux density\" in physics."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::VL5QBNPI";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "integral_wrt_time_of_surface_downwelling_longwave_flux_in_air"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/WSMM/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/D0CRZHK9/>
