        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The surface called \"surface\" means the lower boundary of the atmosphere. \"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area. \"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Xe\" means the element \"xenon\" and \"137Xe\" is the isotope \"xenon-137\" with a half-life of 2.71e-03 days."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::A9G0MM0M";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "surface_radioactivity_content_of_137Xe"@en;
