        skos:definition        "\"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area. The \"atmosphere content\" of a quantity refers to the vertical integral from the surface to the top of the atmosphere. For the content between specified levels in the atmosphere, standard names including \"content_of_atmosphere_layer\" are used. The mass is the total mass of the molecules. The chemical formula for Halon2402 is C2Br2F4. The IUPAC name for Halon2402 is 1,2-dibromo-1,1,2,2-tetrafluoroethane."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CF12N51";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "atmosphere_mass_content_of_halon2402"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/KMP2/> .

