<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N784/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CF12N784";
        dc:date                "2009-07-06 15:41:29.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CF12N784";
        pav:authoredOn         "2009-07-06 15:41:29.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N784/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/tendency_of_ocean_potential_energy_content/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/tendency_of_ocean_potential_energy_content>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "\"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area.  Potential energy is the sum of the gravitational potential energy relative to the geoid and the centripetal potential energy. (The geopotential is the specific potential energy.)  \"tendency_of_X\" means derivative of X with respect to time."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CF12N784";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "tendency_of_ocean_potential_energy_content"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/UFAA/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/8OTRUM79/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::8OTRUM79";
        dc:date                "2018-05-15 09:59:16.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::8OTRUM79";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-05-15 09:59:16.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/8OTRUM79/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/gross_primary_productivity_of_biomass_expressed_as_14C/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/gross_primary_productivity_of_biomass_expressed_as_14C>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "\"Production of carbon\" means the production of biomass expressed as the mass of carbon which it contains. Gross primary production is the rate of synthesis of biomass from inorganic precursors by autotrophs (\"producers\"), for example, photosynthesis in plants or phytoplankton. The producers also respire some of this biomass and the difference is \"net_primary_production\". \"Productivity\" means production per unit area. The phrase \"expressed_as\" is used in the construction A_expressed_as_B, where B is a chemical constituent of A. It means that the quantity indicated by the standard name is calculated solely with respect to the B contained in A, neglecting all other chemical constituents of A. \"C\" means the element carbon and \"14C\" is the radioactive isotope \"carbon-14\", having six protons and eight neutrons and used in radiocarbon dating."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::8OTRUM79";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "gross_primary_productivity_of_biomass_expressed_as_14C"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/KSP2/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/NF56TZGW/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::NF56TZGW";
        dc:date                "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
