<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/WF3PJDFK/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::WF3PJDFK";
        dc:date                "2018-04-16 15:20:49.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::WF3PJDFK";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-04-16 15:20:49.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/WF3PJDFK/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/surface_litter_mass_content_of_nitrogen/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/surface_litter_mass_content_of_nitrogen>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "\"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area. \"Litter\" is dead plant material in or above the soil. It is distinct from coarse wood debris. The precise distinction between \"fine\" and \"coarse\" is model dependent. \"Surface litter\" means the part of the litter resting above the soil surface. The sum of the quantities with standard names wood_debris_mass_content_of_nitrogen, surface_litter_mass_content_of_nitrogen and subsurface_litter_mass_content_of_nitrogen is the total nitrogen mass content of dead plant material."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::WF3PJDFK";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "surface_litter_mass_content_of_nitrogen"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/KMP2/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/FGYJM40L/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::FGYJM40L";
        dc:date                "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::FGYJM40L";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/FGYJM40L/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_97Nb_in_air/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_97Nb_in_air>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The phrase \"integral_wrt_X_of_Y\" means int Y dX. The data variable should have an axis for X specifying the limits of the integral as bounds. The phrase \"wrt\" means \"with respect to\". \"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Radioactivity concentration\" means radioactivity per unit volume of the medium. \"Nb\" means the element \"niobium\" and \"97Nb\" is the isotope \"niobium-97\" with a half-life of 5.11e-02 days."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::FGYJM40L";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_97Nb_in_air"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/BSM3/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/AD85SZNH/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::AD85SZNH";
        dc:date                "2024-05-20 20:39:49.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::AD85SZNH";
        pav:authoredOn         "2024-05-20 20:39:49.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/AD85SZNH/2/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/AD85SZNH/1/>;
        pav:version            "2";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/ratio_of_sea_water_potential_temperature_anomaly_to_relaxation_timescale/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/ratio_of_sea_water_potential_temperature_anomaly_to_relaxation_timescale>;
        owl:versionInfo        "2";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The quantity with standard name ratio_of_sea_water_potential_temperature_anomaly_to_relaxation_timescale is a correction term applied to modelled sea water potential temperature. The term is estimated as the deviation of model local sea water potential temperature from an observation-based climatology (e.g. World Ocean Database) weighted by a user-specified relaxation coefficient in s-1 (1/(relaxation timescale)). Potential temperature is the temperature a parcel of air or sea water would have if moved adiabatically to sea level pressure. The phrase \"ratio_of_X_to_Y\" means X/Y. The term \"anomaly\" means difference from climatology. It is strongly recommended that a variable with this standard name should have the attribute units_metadata=\"temperature: difference\", meaning that it refers to temperature differences and implying that the origin of the temperature scale is irrelevant, because it is essential to know whether a temperature is on-scale or a difference in order to convert the units correctly (cf. https://cfconventions.org/cf-conventions/cf-conventions.html#temperature-units)."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::AD85SZNH";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "ratio_of_sea_water_potential_temperature_anomaly_to_relaxation_timescale"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/KPRS/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/1KY8NWCO/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::1KY8NWCO";
        dc:date                "2017-01-24 16:10:06.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::1KY8NWCO";
        pav:authoredOn         "2017-01-24 16:10:06.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/1KY8NWCO/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/water_flux_into_sea_water_from_land_ice/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/water_flux_into_sea_water_from_land_ice>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "\"Land ice\" means glaciers, ice-caps and ice-sheets resting on bedrock and also includes ice-shelves. In accordance with common usage in geophysical disciplines, \"flux\" implies per unit area, called \"flux density\" in physics. The water flux into sea water from land ice is the freshwater entering the ocean as a result of runoff from the surface and base of the ice and melting from the ice shelf base and vertical ice front. For an area-average, the cell_methods attribute should be used to specify whether the average is over the area of the whole grid cell or the area of the ocean portion only."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::1KY8NWCO";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "water_flux_into_sea_water_from_land_ice"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/KSP2/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N430/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CF12N430";
        dc:date                "2015-01-07 16:23:38.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CF12N430";
        pav:authoredOn         "2015-01-07 16:23:38.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N430/3/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N430/1/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N430/2/>;
        pav:version            "3";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/mole_concentration_of_biogenic_nmvoc_expressed_as_carbon_in_air/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/mole_concentration_of_biogenic_nmvoc_expressed_as_carbon_in_air>;
        owl:versionInfo        "3";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P02/current/OCAA/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P04/current/G141/>;
        skos:definition        "Mole concentration means number of moles per unit volume, also called \"molarity\", and is used in the construction mole_concentration_of_X_in_Y, where X is a material constituent of Y.  A chemical species denoted by X may be described by a single term such as \"nitrogen\" or a phrase such as \"nox_expressed_as_nitrogen\". The phrase \"expressed_as\" is used in the construction A_expressed_as_B, where B is a chemical constituent of A. It means that the quantity indicated by the standard name is calculated solely with respect to the B contained in A, neglecting all other chemical constituents of A. \"nmvoc\" means non methane volatile organic compounds; \"nmvoc\" is the term used in standard names to describe the group of chemical species having this classification that are represented within a given model. The list of individual species that are included in a quantity having a group chemical standard name can vary between models. Where possible, the data variable should be accompanied by a complete description of the species represented, for example, by using a comment attribute. \"Biogenic\" means influenced, caused, or created by natural processes."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CF12N430";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "mole_concentration_of_biogenic_nmvoc_expressed_as_carbon_in_air"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/MLM3/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N223/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CF12N223";
