        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The surface called \"surface\" means the lower boundary of the atmosphere. \"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area. \"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Ce\" means the element \"cerium\" and \"146Ce\" is the isotope \"cerium-146\" with a half-life of 9.86e-03 days."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::VGXTAJQ9";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "surface_radioactivity_content_of_146Ce"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/BQSM/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/UZARDE0R/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::UZARDE0R";
        dc:date                "2023-04-24 17:39:19.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::UZARDE0R";
        pav:authoredOn         "2023-04-24 17:39:19.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/UZARDE0R/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/number_size_distribution_of_cloud_condensation_nuclei_in_air/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/number_size_distribution_of_cloud_condensation_nuclei_in_air>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The cloud condensation nuclei number size distribution is the number concentration of aerosol particles as a function of particle diameter, where the particle acts as condensation nucleus for liquid-phase clouds. A coordinate variable with the standard name of relative_humidity should be specified to indicate that the property refers to a specific supersaturation with respect to liquid water. A coordinate variable with the standard name of electrical_mobility_particle_diameter should be specified to indicate that the property applies at specific mobility particle sizes. To specify the relative humidity at which the particle sizes were selected, provide a scalar coordinate variable with the standard name of relative_humidity_for_aerosol_particle_size_selection. The ability of a particle to act as a condensation nucleus is determined by its size, chemical composition, and morphology."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::UZARDE0R";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "number_size_distribution_of_cloud_condensation_nuclei_in_air"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/PCUM/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/Z1FWE30L/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::Z1FWE30L";
        dc:date                "2018-05-29 16:57:01.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::Z1FWE30L";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-05-29 16:57:01.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/Z1FWE30L/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/upward_transformed_eulerian_mean_air_velocity/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/upward_transformed_eulerian_mean_air_velocity>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "A velocity is a vector quantity. \"Upward\" indicates a vector component which is positive when directed upward (negative downward). Upward air velocity is the vertical component of the 3D air velocity vector. The \"Transformed Eulerian Mean\" refers to a formulation of the mean equations which incorporates some eddy terms into the definition of the mean, described in Andrews et al (1987): Middle Atmospheric Dynamics. Academic Press."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::Z1FWE30L";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "upward_transformed_eulerian_mean_air_velocity"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/UVAA/> .

