<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/24EPBABO/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::24EPBABO";
        dc:date                "2025-05-13 08:28:41.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::24EPBABO";
        pav:authoredOn         "2025-05-13 08:28:41.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/24EPBABO/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/mole_concentration_of_diatoms_expressed_as_silicon_in_sea_water/>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "Mole concentration means number of moles per unit volume, also called \"molarity\", and is used in the construction mole_concentration_of_X_in_Y, where X is a material constituent of Y. A chemical or biological species denoted by X may be described by a single term such as \"nitrogen\" or a phrase such as \"nox_expressed_as_nitrogen\". The phrase \"expressed_as\" is used in the construction A_expressed_as_B, where B is a chemical constituent of A. It means that the quantity indicated by the standard name is calculated in terms of B alone, neglecting all other chemical constituents of A. Diatoms are phytoplankton with an external skeleton made of silica. Phytoplankton are algae that grow where there is sufficient light to support photosynthesis."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::24EPBABO";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "mole_concentration_of_diatoms_expressed_as_silicon_in_sea_water"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/MLM3/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/ZKN4RHCA/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::ZKN4RHCA";
        dc:date                "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::ZKN4RHCA";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/ZKN4RHCA/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_119mIn_in_air/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_119mIn_in_air>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The phrase \"integral_wrt_X_of_Y\" means int Y dX. The data variable should have an axis for X specifying the limits of the integral as bounds. The phrase \"wrt\" means \"with respect to\". \"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Radioactivity concentration\" means radioactivity per unit volume of the medium. \"In\" means the element \"indium\" and \"119mIn\" is the metastable state of the isotope \"indium-119\" with a half-life of 1.25e-02 days."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::ZKN4RHCA";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_119mIn_in_air"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/BSM3/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N34/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CF12N34";
        dc:date                "2009-07-06 15:41:29.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CF12N34";
        pav:authoredOn         "2009-07-06 15:41:29.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N34/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/atmosphere_mass_content_of_chlorine_nitrate/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/atmosphere_mass_content_of_chlorine_nitrate>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P02/current/HLAT/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P04/current/G145/>;
        skos:definition        "\"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area.  The \"atmosphere content\" of a quantity refers to the vertical integral from the surface to the top of the atmosphere. For the content between specified levels in the atmosphere, standard names including content_of_atmosphere_layer are used.  The chemical formula for chlorine nitrate is ClONO2."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CF12N34";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "atmosphere_mass_content_of_chlorine_nitrate"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/KMP2/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0526/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CFSN0526";
        dc:date                "2006-09-26 18:12:43.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CFSN0526";
        pav:authoredOn         "2006-09-26 18:12:43.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0526/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/net_rate_of_absorption_of_longwave_energy_in_atmosphere_layer> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/net_rate_of_absorption_of_longwave_energy_in_atmosphere_layer/>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P04/current/G197/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P64/current/G197/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P64/current/G206/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P04/current/G206/>;
        skos:definition        "'longwave' means longwave radiation. 'Layer' means any layer with upper and lower boundaries that have constant values in some vertical coordinate. There must be a vertical coordinate variable indicating the extent of the layer(s). If the layers are model layers, the vertical coordinate can be model_level_number, but it is recommended to specify a physical coordinate (in a scalar or auxiliary coordinate variable) as well. Net absorbed radiation is the difference between absorbed and emitted radiation."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CFSN0526";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "net_rate_of_absorption_of_longwave_energy_in_atmosphere_layer"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/UFAA/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/7AF3S46U/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::7AF3S46U";
        dc:date                "2025-05-13 08:28:42.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::7AF3S46U";
        pav:authoredOn         "2025-05-13 08:28:42.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/7AF3S46U/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/mole_concentration_of_nanophytoplankton_expressed_as_nitrogen_in_sea_water/>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "Mole concentration means number of moles per unit volume, also called \"molarity\", and is used in the construction mole_concentration_of_X_in_Y, where X is a material constituent of Y. A chemical or biological species denoted by X may be described by a single term such as \"nitrogen\" or a phrase such as \"nox_expressed_as_nitrogen\". The phrase \"expressed_as\" is used in the construction A_expressed_as_B, where B is a chemical constituent of A. It means that the quantity indicated by the standard name is calculated solely with respect to the B contained in A, neglecting all other chemical constituents of A. Nanophytoplankton are phytoplankton between 2 and 20 micrometers in size. Phytoplankton are algae that grow where there is sufficient light to support photosynthesis."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::7AF3S46U";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "mole_concentration_of_nanophytoplankton_expressed_as_nitrogen_in_sea_water"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/MLM3/> .

