        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "\"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Radioactivity concentration\" means radioactivity per unit volume of the medium. \"Xe\" means the element \"xenon\" and \"134mXe\" is the metastable state of the isotope \"xenon-134\" with a half-life of 3.36e-06 days."@en;
