        skos:definition        "The surface called \"surface\" means the lower boundary of the atmosphere. \"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area. \"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Ra\" means the element \"radium\" and \"229Ra\" is the isotope \"radium-229\" with a half-life of 1.16e-17 days."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::3LHWCHI3";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "surface_radioactivity_content_of_229Ra"@en;
