<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/1BQQEFIF/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::1BQQEFIF";
        dc:date                "2025-07-23 16:10:50.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::1BQQEFIF";
        pav:authoredOn         "2025-07-23 16:10:50.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/1BQQEFIF/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/mass_fraction_of_frozen_water_in_air/>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The phrase \"frozen_water\" means ice. \"Mass fraction\" is used in the construction \"mass_fraction_of_X_in_Y\", where X is a material constituent of Y. It means the ratio of the mass of X to the mass of Y (including X). A chemical species or biological group denoted by X may be described by a single term such as \"nitrogen\" or a phrase such as \"nox_expressed_as_nitrogen\"."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::1BQQEFIF";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "mass_fraction_of_frozen_water_in_air"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/UUUU/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N14/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CF12N14";
        dc:date                "2009-07-06 15:41:29.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CF12N14";
        pav:authoredOn         "2009-07-06 15:41:29.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N14/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/atmosphere_mass_content_of_benzene/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/atmosphere_mass_content_of_benzene>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P02/current/OHAT/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P04/current/G140/>;
        skos:definition        "\"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area.  The \"atmosphere content\" of a quantity refers to the vertical integral from the surface to the top of the atmosphere. For the content between specified levels in the atmosphere, standard names including content_of_atmosphere_layer are used.  The chemical formula for benzene is C6H6.  Benzene is the simplest aromatic hydrocarbon and has a ring structure consisting of six carbon atoms joined by alternating single and double chemical bonds. Each carbon atom is additionally bonded to one hydrogen atom. There are standard names that refer to aromatic_compounds as a group, as well as those for individual species."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CF12N14";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "atmosphere_mass_content_of_benzene"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/KMP2/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/VX43SDBZ/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::VX43SDBZ";
        dc:date                "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::VX43SDBZ";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/VX43SDBZ/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_153Sm_in_air/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_153Sm_in_air>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The phrase \"integral_wrt_X_of_Y\" means int Y dX. The data variable should have an axis for X specifying the limits of the integral as bounds. The phrase \"wrt\" means \"with respect to\". \"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Radioactivity concentration\" means radioactivity per unit volume of the medium. \"Sm\" means the element \"samarium\" and \"153Sm\" is the isotope \"samarium-153\" with a half-life of 1.94e+00 days."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::VX43SDBZ";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_153Sm_in_air"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/BSM3/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0415/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CFSN0415";
        dc:date                "2006-09-26 18:12:43.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CFSN0415";
        pav:authoredOn         "2006-09-26 18:12:43.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0415/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/runoff_amount/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/runoff_amount>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P04/current/G661/>;
        skos:definition        "'Amount' means mass per unit area. Runoff is the liquid water which drains from land. If not specified, 'runoff' refers to the sum of surface runoff and subsurface drainage."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CFSN0415";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "runoff_amount"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/KMP2/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/U75LI0LY/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::U75LI0LY";
        dc:date                "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::U75LI0LY";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/U75LI0LY/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_215At_in_air/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_215At_in_air>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The phrase \"integral_wrt_X_of_Y\" means int Y dX. The data variable should have an axis for X specifying the limits of the integral as bounds. The phrase \"wrt\" means \"with respect to\". \"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Radioactivity concentration\" means radioactivity per unit volume of the medium. \"At\" means the element \"astatine\" and \"215At\" is the isotope \"astatine-215\" with a half-life of 1.16e-09 days."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::U75LI0LY";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_215At_in_air"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/BSM3/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/GVM5787K/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::GVM5787K";
        dc:date                "2017-06-26 15:24:29.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::GVM5787K";
        pav:authoredOn         "2017-06-26 15:24:29.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/GVM5787K/3/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/GVM5787K/1/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/GVM5787K/2/>;
        pav:version            "3";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/mass_fraction_of_pm2p5_dry_aerosol_particles_in_air/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/mass_fraction_of_pm2p5_dry_aerosol_particles_in_air>;
        owl:versionInfo        "3";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "Mass fraction is used in the construction \"mass_fraction_of_X_in_Y\", where X is a material constituent of Y. It means the ratio of the mass of X to the mass of Y (including X). A chemical species denoted by X may be described by a single term such as \"nitrogen\" or a phrase such as \"nox_expressed_as_nitrogen\". \"Aerosol\" means the system of suspended liquid or solid particles in air (except cloud droplets) and their carrier gas, the air itself. Aerosol particles take up ambient water (a process known as hygroscopic growth) depending on the relative humidity and the composition of the particles. \"Dry aerosol particles\" means aerosol particles without any water uptake. \"Pm2p5 aerosol\" means atmospheric particulate compounds with an aerodynamic diameter of less than or equal to 2.5 micrometers."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::GVM5787K";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "mass_fraction_of_pm2p5_dry_aerosol_particles_in_air"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/UUUU/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/A8QVMA6Y/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::A8QVMA6Y";
        dc:date                "2024-05-20 20:39:48.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::A8QVMA6Y";
        pav:authoredOn         "2024-05-20 20:39:48.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/A8QVMA6Y/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/volume_scattering_coefficient_of_radiative_flux_in_air_due_to_pm10_dry_aerosol_particles/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/volume_scattering_coefficient_of_radiative_flux_in_air_due_to_pm10_dry_aerosol_particles>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The volume scattering/absorption/attenuation coefficient is the fractional change of radiative flux per unit path length due to the stated process. Coefficients with canonical units of m2 s-1 i.e. multiplied by density have standard names with specific_ instead of volume_. A scattering_angle should not be specified with this quantity. The scattering/absorption/attenuation coefficient is assumed to be an integral over all wavelengths, unless a coordinate of radiation_wavelength is included to specify the wavelength. Radiative flux is the sum of shortwave and longwave radiative fluxes. \"Aerosol\" means the system of suspended liquid or solid particles in air (except cloud droplets) and their carrier gas, the air itself. Aerosol particles take up ambient water (a process known as hygroscopic growth) depending on the relative humidity and the composition of the particles. \"Dry aerosol particles\" means aerosol particles without any water uptake. The specification of a physical process by the phrase \"due_to_\" process means that the quantity named is a single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity named by omitting the phrase. \"Pm10 aerosol particles\" means atmospheric particulate compounds with an aerodynamic diameter of less than or equal to 10 micrometers."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::A8QVMA6Y";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "volume_scattering_coefficient_of_radiative_flux_in_air_due_to_pm10_dry_aerosol_particles"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/UPRM/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/D8RHMOHX/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::D8RHMOHX";
        dc:date                "2021-09-20 14:41:46.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::D8RHMOHX";
        pav:authoredOn         "2021-09-20 14:41:46.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/D8RHMOHX/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/sea_surface_downward_eastward_stress_due_to_dissipation_of_sea_surface_waves/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/sea_surface_downward_eastward_stress_due_to_dissipation_of_sea_surface_waves>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The surface called \"sea surface\" means the upper boundary of the ocean. \"Surface stress\" means the shear stress (force per unit area) exerted at the surface. A downward stress is a downward flux of momentum. Over large bodies of water, surface stress can drive near-surface currents. \"Downward\" indicates a vector component which is positive when directed downward (negative upward). \"Eastward\" indicates a vector component which is positive when directed northward (negative southward). \"Downward eastward\" indicates the ZX component of a tensor. A downward eastward stress is a downward flux of eastward momentum, which accelerates the lower medium eastward and the upper medium westward. The specification of a physical process by the phrase \"due_to_\" process means that the quantity named is a single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity named by omitting the phrase. The phrase \"dissipation_of_sea_surface_waves\" means the stress associated with sea surface waves dissipation processes such as whitecapping."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::D8RHMOHX";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "sea_surface_downward_eastward_stress_due_to_dissipation_of_sea_surface_waves"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/PASX/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/WIMDBQSD/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::WIMDBQSD";
        dc:date                "2018-05-15 09:59:16.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::WIMDBQSD";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-05-15 09:59:16.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/WIMDBQSD/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/solid_precipitation_flux_containing_single_2H/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/solid_precipitation_flux_containing_single_2H>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "In accordance with common usage in geophysical disciplines, \"flux\" implies per unit area, called \"flux density\" in physics. Solid precipitation refers to the precipitation of water in the solid phase. Water in the atmosphere exists in one of three phases: solid, liquid or vapor. The solid phase can exist as snow, hail, graupel, cloud ice, or as a component of aerosol. The chemical formula for water is H2O. \"H\" means the element \"hydrogen\" and \"2H\" is the stable isotope \"hydrogen-2\", usually called \"deuterium\". The construction \"X_containing_single_Y\" means the standard name refers to only that part of X composed of molecules containing a single atom of isotope Y."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::WIMDBQSD";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "solid_precipitation_flux_containing_single_2H"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/KSP2/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0161/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CFSN0161";
        dc:date                "2006-09-26 18:12:43.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CFSN0161";
        pav:authoredOn         "2006-09-26 18:12:43.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0161/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/tendency_of_eastward_wind_due_to_diffusion> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/tendency_of_eastward_wind_due_to_diffusion/>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P02/current/EWSB/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P64/current/G259/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P04/current/G259/>;
        skos:definition        "The specification of a physical process by the phrase due_to_process means that the quantity named is a single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity named by omitting the phrase. 'tendency_of_X' means derivative of X with respect to time. 'Eastward' indicates a vector component which is positive when directed eastward (negative westward). Wind is defined as a two-dimensional (horizontal) air velocity vector, with no vertical component. (Vertical motion in the atmosphere has the standard name upward_air_velocity.)"@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CFSN0161";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "tendency_of_eastward_wind_due_to_diffusion"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/MPS2/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0252/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CFSN0252";
        dc:date                "2021-01-18 16:23:44.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CFSN0252";
        pav:authoredOn         "2021-01-18 16:23:44.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0252/2/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0252/1/>;
        pav:version            "2";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/surface_snow_melt_amount> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/surface_snow_melt_amount/>;
        owl:versionInfo        "2";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P04/current/G523/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P64/current/G523/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P04/current/G646/>;
        skos:definition        "Surface snow refers to the snow on the solid ground or on surface ice cover, but excludes, for example, falling snowflakes and snow on plants. The surface called \"surface\" means the lower boundary of the atmosphere. \"Amount\" means mass per unit area."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CFSN0252";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "surface_snow_melt_amount"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/KMP2/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/K0VS8PV6/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::K0VS8PV6";
        dc:date                "2025-05-13 08:28:42.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::K0VS8PV6";
        pav:authoredOn         "2025-05-13 08:28:42.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/K0VS8PV6/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/ocean_wet_mass_content_of_epipelagic_micronekton/>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "Component of the micronekton that inhabits permanently the epipelagic layer. The epipelagic layer is the ocean layer with light levels sufficient for photosynthesis. \"Wet_mass\" is the mass of a sample before any water has been removed. \"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area. The \"ocean content\" of a quantity refers to the vertical integral within the specified vertical bounds. Micronekton is a group of organisms that range in size from 2 to 20 cm and are capable of swimming independently of ocean currents."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::K0VS8PV6";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "ocean_wet_mass_content_of_epipelagic_micronekton"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/UGMS/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/SPJEJ9XV/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::SPJEJ9XV";
        dc:date                "2026-03-16 11:27:13.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::SPJEJ9XV";
        pav:authoredOn         "2026-03-16 11:27:13.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/SPJEJ9XV/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/ocean_number_content_of_plastic_items/>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "\"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area. The \"ocean content\" of a quantity refers to the vertical integral from the surface to the bottom of the ocean. A plastic item is a synthetic polymer item, usually originating from the fragmentation of larger plastic debris."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::SPJEJ9XV";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "ocean_number_content_of_plastic_items"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/PMSQ/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/7L9HYMBD/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::7L9HYMBD";
        dc:date                "2018-07-03 16:09:23.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::7L9HYMBD";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-07-03 16:09:23.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/7L9HYMBD/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/sea_ice_x_force_per_unit_area_due_to_sea_surface_tilt/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/sea_ice_x_force_per_unit_area_due_to_sea_surface_tilt>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "\"x\" indicates a vector component along the grid x-axis, positive with increasing x. The specification of a physical process by the phrase \"due_to_\" process means that the quantity named is a single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity named by omitting the phrase. Several factors contribute to differences in the ocean surface level, including uneven heating, salinity variations, and currents, especially near coastal regions or ice shelves. Differences in surface level result in sea-surface tilt, a force that influences the ice motion. Reference: National Snow and Ice Data Center https://nsidc.org/cryosphere/seaice/processes/dynamics.html. \"Sea ice\" means all ice floating in the sea which has formed from freezing sea water, rather than by other processes such as calving of land ice to form icebergs."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::7L9HYMBD";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "sea_ice_x_force_per_unit_area_due_to_sea_surface_tilt"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/UNSM/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/PQU4JFOU/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::PQU4JFOU";
        dc:date                "2022-03-18 12:42:55.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::PQU4JFOU";
        pav:authoredOn         "2022-03-18 12:42:55.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/PQU4JFOU/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/mass_concentration_of_prasinoxanthin_in_sea_water/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/mass_concentration_of_prasinoxanthin_in_sea_water>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "\"Mass concentration\" means mass per unit volume and is used in the construction \"mass_concentration_of_X_in_Y\", where X is a material constituent of Y. A chemical species or biological group denoted by X may be described by a single term such as \"nitrogen\" or a phrase such as \"nox_expressed_as_nitrogen\". The chemical formula of prasinoxanthin is C40H56O4. The equivalent term in the NERC P01 Parameter Usage Vocabulary may be found at http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P01/current/PXAPXXXX/2/."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::PQU4JFOU";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "mass_concentration_of_prasinoxanthin_in_sea_water"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/UKMC/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/74B5NJVV/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::74B5NJVV";
        dc:date                "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::74B5NJVV";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/74B5NJVV/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/radioactivity_concentration_of_129Sb_in_air/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/radioactivity_concentration_of_129Sb_in_air>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "\"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Radioactivity concentration\" means radioactivity per unit volume of the medium. \"Sb\" means the element \"antimony\" and \"129Sb\" is the isotope \"antimony-129\" with a half-life of 1.81e-01 days."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::74B5NJVV";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "radioactivity_concentration_of_129Sb_in_air"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/BQM3/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0588/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CFSN0588";
        dc:date                "2013-01-11 16:56:43.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CFSN0588";
        pav:authoredOn         "2013-01-11 16:56:43.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0588/3/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0588/2/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0588/1/>;
        pav:version            "3";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/land_ice_vertical_mean_x_velocity> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/land_ice_vertical_mean_x_velocity/>;
        owl:versionInfo        "3";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P04/current/G495/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P64/current/G495/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P04/current/G611/>;
        skos:definition        "A velocity is a vector quantity. \"x\" indicates a vector component along the grid x-axis, positive with increasing x. \"Land ice\" means glaciers, ice-caps and ice-sheets resting on bedrock and also includes ice-shelves. The vertical mean land ice velocity is the average from the bedrock to the surface of the ice."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CFSN0588";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "land_ice_vertical_mean_x_velocity"@en;
