        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The surface called \"surface\" means the lower boundary of the atmosphere. \"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area. \"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Sr\" means the element \"strontium\" and \"91Sr\" is the isotope \"strontium-91\" with a half-life of 3.95e-01 days."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::EOCDL5SK";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
