<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/UAHJU591/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::UAHJU591";
        dc:date                "2022-03-18 12:42:55.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::UAHJU591";
        pav:authoredOn         "2022-03-18 12:42:55.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/UAHJU591/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/mole_concentration_of_dissolved_nitrogen_in_sea_water/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/mole_concentration_of_dissolved_nitrogen_in_sea_water>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "\"Mole concentration\" means number of moles per unit volume, also called \"molarity\", and is used in the construction \"mole_concentration_of_X_in_Y\", where X is a material constituent of Y. A chemical species or biological group denoted by X may be described by a single term such as \"nitrogen\" or a phrase such as \"nox_expressed_as_nitrogen\". \"Dissolved nitrogen\" means the sum of all nitrogen in solution: inorganic nitrogen (nitrite, nitrate and ammonium) plus nitrogen in carbon compounds."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::UAHJU591";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "mole_concentration_of_dissolved_nitrogen_in_sea_water"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/MLM3/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0439/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CFSN0439";
        dc:date                "2018-10-15 12:56:49.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CFSN0439";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-10-15 12:56:49.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0439/3/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0439/1/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0439/2/>;
        pav:version            "3";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/platform_orientation> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/B39/current/heading/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/platform_orientation/>;
        owl:versionInfo        "3";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P02/current/HEAD/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P04/current/H157/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P64/current/H157/>;
        skos:definition        "Orientation is the clockwise angle with respect to North of the longitudinal (front-to-back) axis of the platform, which may be different to the platform course (which has the standard name platform_course). A \"platform\" is a structure or vehicle that serves as a base for mounting sensors. Platforms include, but are not limited to, satellites, aeroplanes, ships, buoys, instruments, ground stations, and masts."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CFSN0439";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "platform_orientation"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/UAAA/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N646/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CF12N646";
        dc:date                "2009-07-06 15:41:29.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CF12N646";
        pav:authoredOn         "2009-07-06 15:41:29.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N646/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/tendency_of_atmosphere_mass_content_of_molecular_hydrogen_due_to_dry_deposition/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/tendency_of_atmosphere_mass_content_of_molecular_hydrogen_due_to_dry_deposition>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "\"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area.  The \"atmosphere content\" of a quantity refers to the vertical integral from the surface to the top of the atmosphere. For the content between specified levels in the atmosphere, standard names including content_of_atmosphere_layer are used.  The specification of a physical process by the phrase due_to_process means that the quantity named is a  single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity  named by omitting the phrase.  \"tendency_of_X\" means derivative of X with respect to time.  \"Dry deposition\" is the sum of turbulent deposition and gravitational settling. The chemical formula for molecular hydrogen is H2."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CF12N646";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "tendency_of_atmosphere_mass_content_of_molecular_hydrogen_due_to_dry_deposition"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/KSP2/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/69ZBE698/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::69ZBE698";
        dc:date                "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::69ZBE698";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/69ZBE698/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_239U_in_air/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_239U_in_air>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The phrase \"integral_wrt_X_of_Y\" means int Y dX. The data variable should have an axis for X specifying the limits of the integral as bounds. The phrase \"wrt\" means \"with respect to\". \"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Radioactivity concentration\" means radioactivity per unit volume of the medium. \"U\" means the element \"uranium\" and \"239U\" is the isotope \"uranium-239\" with a half-life of 1.63e-02 days."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::69ZBE698";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_239U_in_air"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/BSM3/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/AJAJCJAA/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::AJAJCJAA";
        dc:date                "2013-02-12 14:24:58.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::AJAJCJAA";
        pav:authoredOn         "2013-02-12 14:24:58.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/AJAJCJAA/2/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/AJAJCJAA/1/>;
        pav:version            "2";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/tendency_of_atmosphere_mass_content_of_methane_due_to_emission_from_industrial_processes_and_combustion/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/tendency_of_atmosphere_mass_content_of_methane_due_to_emission_from_industrial_processes_and_combustion>;
        owl:versionInfo        "2";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P02/current/AALK/>;
        skos:definition        "\"tendency_of_X\" means derivative of X with respect to time. \"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area. The \"atmosphere content\" of a quantity refers to the vertical integral from the surface to the top of the atmosphere. For the content between specified levels in the atmosphere, standard names including \"content_of_atmosphere_layer\" are used. The mass is the total mass of the molecules. The specification of a physical process by the phrase \"due_to_\" process means that the quantity named is a single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity named by omitting the phrase. \"Emission\" means emission from a primary source located anywhere within the atmosphere, including at the lower boundary (i.e. earth&amp;apos;s surface). \"Emission\" is a process entirely distinct from \"re-emission\" which is used in some standard names. The chemical formula for methane is CH4. Methane is a member of the group of hydrocarbons known as alkanes. There are standard names for the alkane group as well as for some of the individual species. The \"industrial processes and combustion\" sector comprises fuel combustion activities related to manufacturing industries and construction, industrial processes related to mineral products, the chemical industry, metal production, the production of pulp, paper, food and drink, and non-energy industry use of lubricants and waxes. It may also include any not-classified or \"other\" combustion, which is commonly included in industry-related inventory data. \"Industrial processes and combustion\" is the term used in standard names to describe a collection of emission sources. A variable which has this value for the standard_name attribute should be accompanied by a comment attribute which lists the source categories and provides a reference to the categorization scheme, for example, \"IPCC (Intergovernmental Panel on Climate Change) source categories 1A2, 2A, 2B, 2C, 2D and 2G as defined in the 2006 IPCC guidelines for national greenhouse gas inventories\"."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::AJAJCJAA";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "tendency_of_atmosphere_mass_content_of_methane_due_to_emission_from_industrial_processes_and_combustion"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/KSP2/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/4KYNIHSD/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::4KYNIHSD";
        dc:date                "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::4KYNIHSD";
