        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_162Gd_in_air/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_162Gd_in_air>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The phrase \"integral_wrt_X_of_Y\" means int Y dX. The data variable should have an axis for X specifying the limits of the integral as bounds. The phrase \"wrt\" means \"with respect to\". \"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Radioactivity concentration\" means radioactivity per unit volume of the medium. \"Gd\" means the element \"gadolinium\" and \"162Gd\" is the isotope \"gadolinium-162\" with a half-life of 6.92e-03 days."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::0U71GV1I";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_162Gd_in_air"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/BSM3/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0206/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CFSN0206";
        dc:date                "2024-05-20 20:39:49.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CFSN0206";
        pav:authoredOn         "2024-05-20 20:39:49.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0206/2/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0206/1/>;
        pav:version            "2";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/tendency_of_air_temperature_due_to_dry_convection> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/tendency_of_air_temperature_due_to_dry_convection/>;
        owl:versionInfo        "2";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P04/current/G233/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P64/current/G233/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P02/current/CDTA/>;
        skos:definition        "The specification of a physical process by the phrase due_to_process means that the quantity named is a single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity named by omitting the phrase. \"tendency_of_X\" means derivative of X with respect to time. Air temperature is the bulk temperature of the air, not the surface (skin) temperature. It is strongly recommended that a variable with this standard name should have the attribute units_metadata=\"temperature: difference\", meaning that it refers to temperature differences and implying that the origin of the temperature scale is irrelevant, because it is essential to know whether a temperature is on-scale or a difference in order to convert the units correctly (cf. https://cfconventions.org/cf-conventions/cf-conventions.html#temperature-units)."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CFSN0206";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "tendency_of_air_temperature_due_to_dry_convection"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/KPRS/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/JG8UUOE9/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::JG8UUOE9";
        dc:date                "2018-12-17 17:17:12.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::JG8UUOE9";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-12-17 17:17:12.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/JG8UUOE9/3/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/JG8UUOE9/1/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/JG8UUOE9/2/>;
        pav:version            "3";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/partial_pressure_of_carbon_dioxide_in_sea_water/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/partial_pressure_of_carbon_dioxide_in_sea_water>;
        owl:versionInfo        "3";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The partial pressure of a dissolved gas in sea water is the partial pressure in air with which it would be in equilibrium. The partial pressure of a gaseous constituent of air is the pressure that it would exert if all other gaseous constituents were removed, assuming the volume, the temperature, and its number of moles remain unchanged. The chemical formula for carbon dioxide is CO2."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::JG8UUOE9";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "partial_pressure_of_carbon_dioxide_in_sea_water"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/PASX/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/8WQBU9D0/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::8WQBU9D0";
        dc:date                "2024-09-04 12:51:21.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::8WQBU9D0";
        pav:authoredOn         "2024-09-04 12:51:21.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/8WQBU9D0/3/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/8WQBU9D0/1/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/8WQBU9D0/2/>;
        pav:version            "3";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/radio_signal_roundtrip_travel_time_in_air/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/radio_signal_roundtrip_travel_time_in_air>;
        owl:versionInfo        "3";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The \"instrument\" (examples are radar and lidar) is the device used to make the observation. The \"scatterers\" are what causes the transmitted signal to be returned to the instrument (examples are aerosols, hydrometeors and refractive index irregularities), of whatever kind the instrument detects. A standard name referring to time taken for a signal to propagate from the emitting instrument to a reflecting volume and back again to the instrument."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::8WQBU9D0";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "radio_signal_roundtrip_travel_time_in_air"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/UTBB/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/E8SXAB5A/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::E8SXAB5A";
        dc:date                "2015-01-07 16:23:38.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::E8SXAB5A";
        pav:authoredOn         "2015-01-07 16:23:38.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/E8SXAB5A/2/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/E8SXAB5A/1/>;
        pav:version            "2";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/tendency_of_atmosphere_mass_content_of_nox_expressed_as_nitrogen_monoxide_due_to_emission_from_soil/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/tendency_of_atmosphere_mass_content_of_nox_expressed_as_nitrogen_monoxide_due_to_emission_from_soil>;
        owl:versionInfo        "2";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "\"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area. The \"atmosphere content\" of a quantity refers to the vertical integral from the surface to the top of the atmosphere. For the content between specified levels in the atmosphere, standard names including \"content_of_atmosphere_layer\" are used. The phrase \"expressed_as\" is used in the construction A_expressed_as_B, where B is a chemical constituent of A. It means that the quantity indicated by the standard name is calculated solely with respect to the B contained in A, neglecting all other chemical constituents of A. The specification of a physical process by the phrase \"due_to_\" process means that the quantity named is a single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity named by omitting the phrase. \"Emission\" means emission from a primary source located anywhere within the atmosphere, including at the lower boundary (i.e. the surface of the earth). \"Emission\" is a process entirely distinct from \"re-emission\" which is used in some standard names. \"tendency_of_X\" means derivative of X with respect to time. The chemical formula for nitrogen monoxide is NO. \"Nox\" means a combination of two radical species containing nitrogen and oxygen NO+NO2."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::E8SXAB5A";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "tendency_of_atmosphere_mass_content_of_nox_expressed_as_nitrogen_monoxide_due_to_emission_from_soil"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/KSP2/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/QE4ZQEE7/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::QE4ZQEE7";
        dc:date                "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::QE4ZQEE7";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
