<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/O6T3KQX5/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::O6T3KQX5";
        dc:date                "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::O6T3KQX5";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/O6T3KQX5/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_91Sr_in_air/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_91Sr_in_air>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The phrase \"integral_wrt_X_of_Y\" means int Y dX. The data variable should have an axis for X specifying the limits of the integral as bounds. The phrase \"wrt\" means \"with respect to\". \"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Radioactivity concentration\" means radioactivity per unit volume of the medium. \"Sr\" means the element \"strontium\" and \"91Sr\" is the isotope \"strontium-91\" with a half-life of 3.95e-01 days."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::O6T3KQX5";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_91Sr_in_air"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/BSM3/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV13N11/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CFV13N11";
        dc:date                "2021-09-20 14:41:46.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CFV13N11";
        pav:authoredOn         "2021-09-20 14:41:46.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV13N11/2/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV13N11/1/>;
        pav:version            "2";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/number_of_days_with_air_temperature_above_threshold/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/number_of_days_with_air_temperature_above_threshold>;
        owl:versionInfo        "2";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "Air temperature is the bulk temperature of the air, not the surface (skin) temperature. A variable whose standard name has the form number_of_days_with_X_below|above_threshold is a count of the number of days on which the condition X_below|above_threshold is satisfied. It must have a coordinate variable or scalar coordinate variable with the standard name of X to supply the threshold(s). It must have a climatological time variable, and a cell_methods entry for within days which describes the processing of quantity X before the threshold is applied. A number_of_days is an extensive quantity in time, and the cell_methods entry for over days should be \"sum\"."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CFV13N11";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "number_of_days_with_air_temperature_above_threshold"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/UUUU/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/99X0NGKG/>
