        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The surface called \"surface\" means the lower boundary of the atmosphere. \"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area. \"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"I\" means the element \"iodine\" and \"132I\" is the isotope \"iodine-132\" with a half-life of 9.60e-02 days."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::WQNRZQG1";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
