        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The surface called \"surface\" means the lower boundary of the atmosphere. \"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area. \"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Cs\" means the element \"cesium\" and \"138Cs\" is the isotope \"cesium-138\" with a half-life of 2.23e-02 days."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::RPPL9QNU";
