        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The surface called \"surface\" means the lower boundary of the atmosphere. \"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area. \"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Th\" means the element \"thorium\" and \"231Th\" is the isotope \"thorium-231\" with a half-life of 1.06e+00 days."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::FMTSIANA";
