        skos:definition        "The surface called \"surface\" means the lower boundary of the atmosphere. \"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area. \"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Pr\" means the element \"praseodymium\" and \"145Pr\" is the isotope \"praseodymium-145\" with a half-life of 2.49e-01 days."@en;
