<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/DBRHUQ8Q/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::DBRHUQ8Q";
        dc:date                "2024-05-20 20:39:48.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::DBRHUQ8Q";
        pav:authoredOn         "2024-05-20 20:39:48.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/DBRHUQ8Q/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/volume_backwards_scattering_coefficient_of_radiative_flux_in_air_due_to_pm10_aerosol_particles_at_standard_temperature_and_pressure/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/volume_backwards_scattering_coefficient_of_radiative_flux_in_air_due_to_pm10_aerosol_particles_at_standard_temperature_and_pressure>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The volume scattering/absorption/attenuation coefficient is the fractional change of radiative flux per unit path length due to the stated process. Coefficients with canonical units of m2 s-1 i.e. multiplied by density have standard names with specific_ instead of volume_. Backwards scattering refers to the sum of scattering into all backward angles i.e. scattering_angle exceeds pi/2 radians. A scattering_angle should not be specified with this quantity. The scattering/absorption/attenuation coefficient is assumed to be an integral over all wavelengths, unless a coordinate of radiation_wavelength is included to specify the wavelength. Radiative flux is the sum of shortwave and longwave radiative fluxes. \"Aerosol\" means the system of suspended liquid or solid particles in air (except cloud droplets) and their carrier gas, the air itself. To specify the relative humidity at which the sample was measured, provide a scalar coordinate variable with the standard name of \"relative_humidity\". The specification of a physical process by the phrase \"due_to_\" process means that the quantity named is a single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity named by omitting the phrase. \"Pm10 aerosol particles\" means atmospheric particulate compounds with an aerodynamic diameter of less than or equal to 10 micrometers. \"Standard_temperature_and_pressure\" refer to a reference volume at 273.15 K temperature and 1013.25 hPa pressure."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::DBRHUQ8Q";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "volume_backwards_scattering_coefficient_of_radiative_flux_in_air_due_to_pm10_aerosol_particles_at_standard_temperature_and_pressure"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/UPRM/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N169/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CF12N169";
        dc:date                "2009-07-06 15:41:29.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CF12N169";
        pav:authoredOn         "2009-07-06 15:41:29.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N169/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/atmosphere_moles_of_nox_expressed_as_nitrogen/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/atmosphere_moles_of_nox_expressed_as_nitrogen>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P02/current/AAMN/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P04/current/G161/>;
        skos:definition        "The construction \"atmosphere_moles_of_X\" means the total number of moles of X in the entire atmosphere, i.e. summed over the atmospheric column and over the entire globe. \"Nox\" means a combination of two radical species containing nitrogen and oxygen: NO+NO2. The phrase 'expressed_as' is used in the construction A_expressed_as_B, where B is a chemical constituent of A. It means that the quantity indicated by the standard name is calculated solely with respect to the B contained in A, neglecting all other chemical constituents of A."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CF12N169";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "atmosphere_moles_of_nox_expressed_as_nitrogen"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/MOLE/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/U8UBHA8D/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::U8UBHA8D";
        dc:date                "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::U8UBHA8D";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/U8UBHA8D/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/radioactivity_concentration_of_135I_in_air/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/radioactivity_concentration_of_135I_in_air>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "\"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Radioactivity concentration\" means radioactivity per unit volume of the medium. \"I\" means the element \"iodine\" and \"135I\" is the isotope \"iodine-135\" with a half-life of 2.79e-01 days."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::U8UBHA8D";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "radioactivity_concentration_of_135I_in_air"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/BQM3/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/OC8HSAPJ/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::OC8HSAPJ";
        dc:date                "2019-03-04 17:29:46.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::OC8HSAPJ";
        pav:authoredOn         "2019-03-04 17:29:46.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/OC8HSAPJ/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/toa_outgoing_radiance_per_unit_wavelength_due_to_solar_induced_fluorescence/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/toa_outgoing_radiance_per_unit_wavelength_due_to_solar_induced_fluorescence>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The abbreviation \"toa\" means top of atmosphere. Radiance is the radiative flux in a particular direction, per unit of solid angle. The direction towards which it is going must be specified, for instance with a coordinate of zenith_angle. A coordinate variable for radiation wavelength should be given the standard name radiation_wavelength. The specification of a physical process by the phrase \"due_to_\" process means that the quantity named is a single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity named by omitting the phrase. Some of the solar energy absorbed by pigment systems of plant leaves during photosynthesis is re-emitted as fluorescence. This is called solar-induced chlorophyll fluorescence (SIF). It is a radiance that can be measured on a global scale at various wavelengths and by multiple space borne instruments. SIF is considered a measurement of the photosynthetic machinery in plants and can provide a direct approach for the diagnosis of the actual functional status of vegetation. It is therefore considered a functional proxy of terrestrial gross primary productivity which has the standard name gross_primary_productivity_of_biomass_expressed_as_carbon. SIF spans the wavelength range 600 - 800 nm."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::OC8HSAPJ";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "toa_outgoing_radiance_per_unit_wavelength_due_to_solar_induced_fluorescence"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/WM2S/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/YEQTT04J/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::YEQTT04J";
        dc:date                "2025-05-13 08:28:42.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::YEQTT04J";
        pav:authoredOn         "2025-05-13 08:28:42.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/YEQTT04J/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/sea_floor_horizontal_stress_due_to_sea_surface_waves/>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "Ocean processes such as waves and currents can generate forces (or stress) on the sea floor. The surface called \"sea floor\" means the lower boundary of the ocean. \"Horizontal\" refers to the local horizontal, i.e. perpendicular to the local gravity vector at the location in which the quantity is calculated. \"Stress\" means the shear stress (force per unit area) exerted at the sea floor. Horizontal stress refers to the stress in the horizontal plane. The specification of a physical process by the phrase \"due_to_\" process means that the quantity named is a single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity named by omitting the phrase. The phrase \"sea_surface_waves\" means the stress associated with sea surface waves dissipation processes through bottom friction."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::YEQTT04J";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "sea_floor_horizontal_stress_due_to_sea_surface_waves"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/UNSM/> .

