        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The trough is the lowest point of a wave. Trough depth is the vertical distance between the trough and the calm sea surface. Maximum trough depth is the maximum value measured during the observation period."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::IWJNFWBF";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "sea_surface_wave_maximum_trough_depth"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/ULAA/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/S5CTJ86W/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::S5CTJ86W";
        dc:date                "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::S5CTJ86W";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/S5CTJ86W/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_134Te_in_air/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_134Te_in_air>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The phrase \"integral_wrt_X_of_Y\" means int Y dX. The data variable should have an axis for X specifying the limits of the integral as bounds. The phrase \"wrt\" means \"with respect to\". \"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Radioactivity concentration\" means radioactivity per unit volume of the medium. \"Te\" means the element \"tellurium\" and \"134Te\" is the isotope \"tellurium-134\" with a half-life of 2.92e-02 days."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::S5CTJ86W";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_134Te_in_air"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/BSM3/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/TQEV2Y7Y/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::TQEV2Y7Y";
        dc:date                "2016-04-05 15:08:52.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::TQEV2Y7Y";
        pav:authoredOn         "2016-04-05 15:08:52.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/TQEV2Y7Y/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/northward_northward_derivative_of_geopotential/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/northward_northward_derivative_of_geopotential>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P02/current/GRAV/>;
        skos:definition        "A quantity with standard name Xward_Yward_derivative_of_geopotential is a second spatial derivative of geopotential, P, in the direction specified by X and Y, i.e., d2P/dXdY. Geopotential is the sum of the specific gravitational potential energy relative to the geoid and the specific centripetal potential energy. \"Northward\" indicates a vector component which is positive when directed northward (negative southward). \"component_derivative_of_X\" means derivative of X with respect to distance in the component direction, which may be \"northward\", \"southward\", \"eastward\", \"westward\", \"x\" or \"y\". The last two indicate derivatives along the axes of the grid, in the case where they are not true longitude and latitude."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::TQEV2Y7Y";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "northward_northward_derivative_of_geopotential"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/UPSS/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/TXGHQXIF/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::TXGHQXIF";
        dc:date                "2026-03-16 11:27:13.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::TXGHQXIF";
        pav:authoredOn         "2026-03-16 11:27:13.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/TXGHQXIF/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/canopy_resistance_to_evapotranspiration/>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "Canopy resistance to evapotranspiration is the overall resistance to water vapor transfer from a vegetated canopy to the atmosphere. It incorporates the effects of stomatal resistance (vapor transfer from inside the leaf to its surface), leaf boundary layer resistance (vapor transfer from the leaf surface to the surrounding canopy air), and canopy structure (e.g. multiple canopy layers). \"Evapotranspiration\" means all water vapor fluxes into the atmosphere from the surface: liquid evaporation, sublimation and transpiration. The canopy is often considered to be the outer surfaces of the vegetation. Plant height and the distribution, orientation and shape of plant leaves within a canopy influence the atmospheric environment and many plant processes within the canopy. Reference: AMS Glossary http://glossary.ametsoc.org/wiki/Canopy."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::TXGHQXIF";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "canopy_resistance_to_evapotranspiration"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/SCPM/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/J57FPBOP/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::J57FPBOP";
        dc:date                "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::J57FPBOP";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/J57FPBOP/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/surface_radioactivity_content_of_112Ag/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/surface_radioactivity_content_of_112Ag>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The surface called \"surface\" means the lower boundary of the atmosphere. \"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area. \"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Ag\" means the element \"silver\" and \"112Ag\" is the isotope \"silver-112\" with a half-life of 1.30e-01 days."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::J57FPBOP";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "surface_radioactivity_content_of_112Ag"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/BQSM/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/717J48JP/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::717J48JP";
        dc:date                "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::717J48JP";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/717J48JP/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/radioactivity_concentration_of_118In_in_air/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/radioactivity_concentration_of_118In_in_air>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "\"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Radioactivity concentration\" means radioactivity per unit volume of the medium. \"In\" means the element \"indium\" and \"118In\" is the isotope \"indium-118\" with a half-life of 5.77e-05 days."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::717J48JP";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "radioactivity_concentration_of_118In_in_air"@en;
