        skos:definition        "\"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Radioactivity concentration\" means radioactivity per unit volume of the medium. \"La\" means the element \"lanthanum\" and \"142La\" is the isotope \"lanthanum-142\" with a half-life of 6.42e-02 days."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::VHPE4HO5";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "radioactivity_concentration_of_142La_in_air"@en;
