<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/0NGA1E0E/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::0NGA1E0E";
        dc:date                "2018-12-17 17:17:12.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::0NGA1E0E";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-12-17 17:17:12.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/0NGA1E0E/2/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/0NGA1E0E/1/>;
        pav:version            "2";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/tendency_of_mole_concentration_of_particulate_organic_matter_expressed_as_carbon_in_sea_water_due_to_grazing_of_phytoplankton/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/tendency_of_mole_concentration_of_particulate_organic_matter_expressed_as_carbon_in_sea_water_due_to_grazing_of_phytoplankton>;
        owl:versionInfo        "2";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The phrase \"tendency_of_X\" means derivative of X with respect to time. Mole concentration means number of moles per unit volume, also called \"molarity\", and is used in the construction \"mole_concentration_of_X_in_Y\", where X is a material constituent of Y. A chemical or biological species denoted by X may be described by a single term such as \"nitrogen\" or a phrase such as \"nox_expressed_as_nitrogen\". The phrase \"expressed_as\" is used in the construction A_expressed_as_B, where B is a chemical constituent of A. It means that the quantity indicated by the standard name is calculated solely with respect to the B contained in A, neglecting all other chemical constituents of A. The specification of a physical process by the phrase \"due_to_\" process means that the quantity named is a single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity named by omitting the phrase. Phytoplankton are algae that grow where there is sufficient light to support photosynthesis. \"Grazing of phytoplankton\" means the grazing of phytoplankton by zooplankton."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::0NGA1E0E";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "tendency_of_mole_concentration_of_particulate_organic_matter_expressed_as_carbon_in_sea_water_due_to_grazing_of_phytoplankton"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/MM3S/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N752/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CF12N752";
        dc:date                "2009-07-06 15:41:29.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CF12N752";
        pav:authoredOn         "2009-07-06 15:41:29.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N752/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/tendency_of_mass_fraction_of_stratiform_cloud_condensed_water_in_air_due_to_autoconversion_to_snow/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/tendency_of_mass_fraction_of_stratiform_cloud_condensed_water_in_air_due_to_autoconversion_to_snow>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "Mass fraction is used in the construction mass_fraction_of_X_in_Y, where X is a material constituent of Y. It means the ratio of the mass of X to the mass of Y (including X).  A chemical species denoted by X may be described by a single term such as 'nitrogen' or a phrase such as 'nox_expressed_as_nitrogen'. Autoconversion is the process of collision and coalescence which results in the formation of precipitation particles from cloud water droplets or ice crystals. In an atmosphere model, stratiform cloud is that produced by large-scale convergence (not the convection schemes).  The specification of a physical process by the phrase due_to_process means that the quantity named is a  single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity  named by omitting the phrase.  \"tendency_of_X\" means derivative of X with respect to time.  \"condensed_water\" means liquid and ice."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CF12N752";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "tendency_of_mass_fraction_of_stratiform_cloud_condensed_water_in_air_due_to_autoconversion_to_snow"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/PRSC/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/SU2619C1/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::SU2619C1";
        dc:date                "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::SU2619C1";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/SU2619C1/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_245Cm_in_air/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_245Cm_in_air>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The phrase \"integral_wrt_X_of_Y\" means int Y dX. The data variable should have an axis for X specifying the limits of the integral as bounds. The phrase \"wrt\" means \"with respect to\". \"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Radioactivity concentration\" means radioactivity per unit volume of the medium. \"Cm\" means the element \"curium\" and \"245Cm\" is the isotope \"curium-245\" with a half-life of 3.40e+06 days."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::SU2619C1";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_245Cm_in_air"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/BSM3/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/QY06XVNL/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::QY06XVNL";
        dc:date                "2026-09-15 05:36:52.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::QY06XVNL";
        pav:authoredOn         "2026-09-15 05:36:52.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/QY06XVNL/2/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/QY06XVNL/1/>;
        pav:version            "2";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/ocean_mass_content_of_bathypelagic_fish_expressed_as_wet_weight/>;
        owl:versionInfo        "2";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "\"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area. Bathypelagic fish are deep-sea fish that live at depths of about 1000-3000 m in cold and dark waters. The phrase \"expressed_as\" is used in the construction \"A_expressed_as_B\", where B is a chemical constituent of A. It means that the quantity indicated by the standard name is calculated solely with respect to the B contained in A, neglecting all other chemical constituents of A. Wet weight is the weight of a material, organism, or sample including its water (moisture) content, measured before drying."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::QY06XVNL";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "ocean_mass_content_of_bathypelagic_fish_expressed_as_wet_weight"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/UGMS/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV13N3/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CFV13N3";
        dc:date                "2010-03-11 14:38:28.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CFV13N3";
        pav:authoredOn         "2010-03-11 14:38:28.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV13N3/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/atmosphere_net_upward_shallow_convective_mass_flux/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/atmosphere_net_upward_shallow_convective_mass_flux>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "\"Upward\" indicates a vector component which is positive when directed upward (negative downward).  In accordance with common usage in geophysical disciplines, \"flux\" implies per unit area, called \"flux density\" in physics.  The atmosphere convective mass flux is the vertical transport of mass for a field of cumulus clouds or thermals, given by the product of air density and vertical velocity. For an area-average, cell_methods should specify whether the average is over all the area or the area of updrafts and/or downdrafts only.  Net upward convective mass flux is the difference between the updraft mass flux and the downdraft mass flux."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CFV13N3";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "atmosphere_net_upward_shallow_convective_mass_flux"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/KSP2/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/2L35FZAW/>
