        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The surface called \"surface\" means the lower boundary of the atmosphere. \"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area. \"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Br\" means the element \"bromine\" and \"83Br\" is the isotope \"bromine-83\" with a half-life of 1.00e-01 days."@en;
