        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The surface called \"surface\" means the lower boundary of the atmosphere. \"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area. \"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Bi\" means the element \"bismuth\" and \"212Bi\" is the isotope \"bismuth-212\" with a half-life of 4.20e-02 days."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::6YCFS72W";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "surface_radioactivity_content_of_212Bi"@en;
