        skos:definition        "\"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Radioactivity concentration\" means radioactivity per unit volume of the medium. \"Hg\" means the element \"mercury\" and \"206Hg\" is the isotope \"mercury-206\" with a half-life of 5.57e-03 days."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::31IY1T9C";
