<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV8NS4/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CFV8NS4";
        dc:date                "2017-06-26 15:24:29.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CFV8NS4";
        dc:replaces            <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0781/>;
        pav:authoredOn         "2017-06-26 15:24:29.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV8NS4/3/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV8NS4/2/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV8NS4/1/>;
        pav:version            "3";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/surface_geostrophic_northward_sea_water_velocity> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/surface_geostrophic_northward_sea_water_velocity/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0781/>;
        owl:versionInfo        "3";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P02/current/RFVL/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P04/current/G920/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P64/current/G920/>;
        skos:definition        "The surface called \"surface\" means the lower boundary of the atmosphere. A velocity is a vector quantity. \"Northward\" indicates a vector component which is positive when directed northward (negative southward). \"Geostrophic\" indicates that geostrophic balance is assumed, i.e. that the pressure gradient force and the Coriolis force are balanced and the large scale fluid flow is parallel to the isobars. The quantity with standard name surface_geostrophic_northward_sea_water_velocity is the sum of a variable part, surface_geostrophic_northward_sea_water_velocity_assuming_mean_sea_level_for_geoid, and a constant part due to the stationary component of ocean circulation."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CFV8NS4";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "surface_geostrophic_northward_sea_water_velocity"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/UVAA/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0781/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CFSN0781";
        dc:date                "2008-04-15 14:00:00.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CFSN0781";
        dc:isReplacedBy        <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV8NS4/>;
        pav:authoredOn         "2008-04-15 14:00:00.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0781/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "true";
        owl:sameAs             <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/surface_northward_geostrophic_sea_water_velocity> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV8NS4/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/surface_northward_geostrophic_sea_water_velocity/>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P02/current/RFVL/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P04/current/G920/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P64/current/G920/>;
        skos:definition        "The surface called \"surface\" means the lower boundary of the atmosphere. A velocity is a vector quantity. \"Northward\" indicates a vector component which is positive when directed northward (negative southward). \"Geostrophic\" indicates that geostrophic balance is assumed. \"Water\" means water in all phases. surface_northward_sea_water_geostrophic_velocity is the sum of a variable part, surface_northward_sea_water_geostrophic_velocity_assuming_sea_level_for_geoid, and a constant part due to the stationary component of ocean circulation."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CFSN0781";
        skos:note              "deprecated"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "surface_northward_geostrophic_sea_water_velocity"@en .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/FKYU37Q4/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::FKYU37Q4";
        dc:date                "2024-05-20 20:39:48.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::FKYU37Q4";
        pav:authoredOn         "2024-05-20 20:39:48.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/FKYU37Q4/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/volume_absorption_coefficient_of_radiative_flux_in_air_due_to_ambient_aerosol_particles/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/volume_absorption_coefficient_of_radiative_flux_in_air_due_to_ambient_aerosol_particles>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The volume scattering/absorption/attenuation coefficient is the fractional change of radiative flux per unit path length due to the stated process. Coefficients with canonical units of m2 s-1 i.e. multiplied by density have standard names with specific_ instead of volume_. A scattering_angle should not be specified with this quantity. The scattering/absorption/attenuation coefficient is assumed to be an integral over all wavelengths, unless a coordinate of radiation_wavelength is included to specify the wavelength. Radiative flux is the sum of shortwave and longwave radiative fluxes. \"Aerosol\" means the system of suspended liquid or solid particles in air (except cloud droplets) and their carrier gas, the air itself. \"Ambient aerosol particles\" are aerosol particles that have taken up ambient water through hygroscopic growth. The extent of hygroscopic growth depends on the relative humidity and the composition of the particles. To specify the relative humidity at which the sample was measured, provide a scalar coordinate variable with the standard name of \"relative_humidity\". The specification of a physical process by the phrase \"due_to_\" process means that the quantity named is a single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity named by omitting the phrase."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::FKYU37Q4";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "volume_absorption_coefficient_of_radiative_flux_in_air_due_to_ambient_aerosol_particles"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/UPRM/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/094YNDL9/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::094YNDL9";
        dc:date                "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::094YNDL9";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/094YNDL9/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/radioactivity_concentration_of_246Cm_in_air/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/radioactivity_concentration_of_246Cm_in_air>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "\"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Radioactivity concentration\" means radioactivity per unit volume of the medium. \"Cm\" means the element \"curium\" and \"246Cm\" is the isotope \"curium-246\" with a half-life of 2.01e+06 days."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::094YNDL9";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "radioactivity_concentration_of_246Cm_in_air"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/BQM3/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/UUR1LV7Z/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::UUR1LV7Z";
