        owl:versionInfo        "2";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P02/current/HLAT/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P04/current/G146/>;
        skos:definition        "Mass concentration\" means mass per unit volume and is used in the construction \"mass_concentration_of_X_in_Y\", where X is a material constituent of Y. A chemical or biological species denoted by X may be described by a single term such as \"nitrogen\" or a phrase such as \"nox_expressed_as_nitrogen\". The chemical formula of CFC11 is CFCl3. The IUPAC name for CFC11 is trichloro(fluoro)methane."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CF12N237";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "mass_concentration_of_cfc11_in_air"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/UKMC/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N590/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CF12N590";
        dc:date                "2009-07-06 15:41:29.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CF12N590";
        pav:authoredOn         "2009-07-06 15:41:29.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N590/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/stratiform_cloud_longwave_emissivity> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/stratiform_cloud_longwave_emissivity/>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P64/current/G266/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P64/current/G206/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P04/current/G206/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P04/current/G266/>;
        skos:definition        "Emissivity is the ratio of the power emitted by an object to the power that would be emitted by a perfect black body having the same temperature as the object. The emissivity is assumed to be an integral over all wavelengths, unless a coordinate of radiation_wavelength or radiation_frequency is included to specify either the wavelength or frequency. In an atmosphere model, stratiform cloud is that produced by large-scale convergence (not the convection schemes).  \"longwave\" means longwave radiation."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CF12N590";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "stratiform_cloud_longwave_emissivity"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/UUUU/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P02/current/LWRD/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/0BCQ2T1Y/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::0BCQ2T1Y";
        dc:date                "2026-06-08 13:55:32.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::0BCQ2T1Y";
        pav:authoredOn         "2026-06-08 13:55:32.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/0BCQ2T1Y/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/tendency_of_atmosphere_mass_content_of_carbon_dioxide_expressed_as_carbon_due_to_emissions_and_surface_fluxes/>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The phrase \"tendency_of_X\" means derivative of X with respect to time. \"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area. The \"atmosphere content\" of a quantity refers to the vertical integral from the surface to the top of the atmosphere. For the content between specified levels in the atmosphere, standard names including \"content_of_atmosphere_layer\" are used. The phrase \"expressed_as\" is used in the construction \"A_expressed_as_B\", where B is a chemical constituent of A. It means that the quantity indicated by the standard name is calculated solely with respect to the B contained in A, neglecting all other chemical constituents of A. The specification of a physical process by the phrase \"due_to_\" process means that the quantity named is a single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity named by omitting the phrase. \"Emission\" means emission from a primary source located anywhere within the atmosphere, including at the lower boundary (i.e. the surface of the earth). \"Emission\" is a process entirely distinct from \"re-emission\" which is used in some standard names. In accordance with common usage in geophysical disciplines, \"flux\" implies per unit area, called \"flux density\" in physics. The surface called \"surface\" means the lower boundary of the atmosphere. The chemical formula for carbon dioxide is CO2."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::0BCQ2T1Y";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "tendency_of_atmosphere_mass_content_of_carbon_dioxide_expressed_as_carbon_due_to_emissions_and_surface_fluxes"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/KSP2/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/AAM0FKLD/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::AAM0FKLD";
        dc:date                "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::AAM0FKLD";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/AAM0FKLD/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_78As_in_air/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_78As_in_air>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The phrase \"integral_wrt_X_of_Y\" means int Y dX. The data variable should have an axis for X specifying the limits of the integral as bounds. The phrase \"wrt\" means \"with respect to\". \"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Radioactivity concentration\" means radioactivity per unit volume of the medium. \"As\" means the element \"arsenic\" and \"78As\" is the isotope \"arsenic-78\" with a half-life of 6.32e-02 days."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::AAM0FKLD";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_78As_in_air"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/BSM3/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0180/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CFSN0180";
        dc:date                "2006-09-26 18:12:43.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CFSN0180";
        pav:authoredOn         "2006-09-26 18:12:43.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0180/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/tendency_of_dry_static_energy_content_of_atmosphere_layer/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/tendency_of_dry_static_energy_content_of_atmosphere_layer>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "'tendency_of_X' means derivative of X with respect to time. 'Content' indicates a quantity per unit area. 'Layer' means any layer with upper and lower boundaries that have constant values in some vertical coordinate. There must be a vertical coordinate variable indicating the extent of the layer(s). If the layers are model layers, the vertical coordinate can be model_level_number, but it is recommended to specify a physical coordinate (in a scalar or auxiliary coordinate variable) as well. Dry static energy is the sum of enthalpy and potential energy (itself the sum of gravitational and centripetal potential energy). Enthalpy can be written either as (1) CpT, where Cp is heat capacity at constant pressure, T is absolute temperature, or (2) U+pV, where U is internal energy, p is pressure and V is volume."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CFSN0180";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "tendency_of_dry_static_energy_content_of_atmosphere_layer"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/UFAA/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N494/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CF12N494";
