<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/JHUWODE6/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::JHUWODE6";
        dc:date                "2018-12-17 17:17:12.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::JHUWODE6";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-12-17 17:17:12.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/JHUWODE6/3/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/JHUWODE6/1/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/JHUWODE6/2/>;
        pav:version            "3";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/surface_carbon_dioxide_abiotic_analogue_partial_pressure_difference_between_sea_water_and_air/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/surface_carbon_dioxide_abiotic_analogue_partial_pressure_difference_between_sea_water_and_air>;
        owl:versionInfo        "3";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The surface called \"surface\" means the lower boundary of the atmosphere. The chemical formula for carbon dioxide is CO2. In ocean biogeochemistry models, an \"abiotic analogue\" is used to simulate the effect on a modelled variable when biological effects on ocean carbon concentration and alkalinity are ignored. The partial pressure of a dissolved gas in sea water is the partial pressure in air with which it would be in equilibrium. The partial pressure of a gaseous constituent of air is the pressure that it would exert if all other gaseous constituents were removed, assuming the volume, the temperature, and its number of moles remain unchanged. The partial pressure difference between sea water and air is positive when the partial pressure of the dissolved gas in sea water is greater than the partial pressure in air."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::JHUWODE6";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "surface_carbon_dioxide_abiotic_analogue_partial_pressure_difference_between_sea_water_and_air"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/PASX/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/R7W0A10C/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::R7W0A10C";
        dc:date                "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::R7W0A10C";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/R7W0A10C/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_103mRh_in_air/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_103mRh_in_air>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The phrase \"integral_wrt_X_of_Y\" means int Y dX. The data variable should have an axis for X specifying the limits of the integral as bounds. The phrase \"wrt\" means \"with respect to\". \"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Radioactivity concentration\" means radioactivity per unit volume of the medium. \"Rh\" means the element \"rhodium\" and \"103mRh\" is the metastable state of the isotope \"rhodium-103\" with a half-life of 3.89e-02 days."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::R7W0A10C";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_103mRh_in_air"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/BSM3/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/ZAO9FNHS/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::ZAO9FNHS";
        dc:date                "2018-07-03 16:09:23.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::ZAO9FNHS";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-07-03 16:09:23.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/ZAO9FNHS/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
