<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/2LNHOBDS/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::2LNHOBDS";
        dc:date                "2021-09-20 14:41:46.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::2LNHOBDS";
        pav:authoredOn         "2021-09-20 14:41:46.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/2LNHOBDS/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/change_in_land_ice_mass/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/change_in_land_ice_mass>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "Zero change in land ice mass is an arbitrary level. \"Land ice\" means glaciers, ice-caps and ice-sheets resting on bedrock and also includes ice-shelves. The horizontal domain over which the quantity is calculated is described by the associated coordinate variables and coordinate bounds or by a coordinate variable or scalar coordinate variable with the standard name of \"region\" supplied according to section 6.1.1 of the CF conventions."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::2LNHOBDS";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "change_in_land_ice_mass"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/KGXX/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/KMQ44QVB/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::KMQ44QVB";
        dc:date                "2023-02-06 17:17:13.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::KMQ44QVB";
        pav:authoredOn         "2023-02-06 17:17:13.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/KMQ44QVB/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/moles_of_particulate_biogenic_silica_per_unit_mass_in_sea_water/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/moles_of_particulate_biogenic_silica_per_unit_mass_in_sea_water>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The construction \"moles_of_X_per_unit_mass_in_Y\" is also called \"molality\" of X in Y, where X is a material constituent of Y. A chemical species or biological group denoted by X may be described by a single term such as \"nitrogen\" or a phrase such as \"nox_expressed_as_nitrogen\". Particulate means suspended solids of all sizes. Biogenic silica is a hydrated form of silica (silicon dioxide) with the chemical formula SiO2.nH2O sometimes referred to as opaline silica or opal. It is created by biological processes and in sea water it is predominantly the skeletal material of diatoms."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::KMQ44QVB";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "moles_of_particulate_biogenic_silica_per_unit_mass_in_sea_water"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/MLKG/> .

