<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N92/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CF12N92";
        dc:date                "2019-03-04 17:29:46.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CF12N92";
        pav:authoredOn         "2019-03-04 17:29:46.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N92/2/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N92/1/>;
        pav:version            "2";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/atmosphere_mass_content_of_peroxy_radicals/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/atmosphere_mass_content_of_peroxy_radicals>;
        owl:versionInfo        "2";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "\"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area. The \"atmosphere content\" of a quantity refers to the vertical integral from the surface to the top of the atmosphere. For the content between specified levels in the atmosphere, standard names including \"content_of_atmosphere_layer\" are used. The term \"peroxy_radicals\" means all organic and inorganic peroxy radicals. This includes HO2 and all organic peroxy radicals, sometimes referred to as RO2. In chemistry, a \"radical\" is a highly reactive, and therefore short lived, species."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CF12N92";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "atmosphere_mass_content_of_peroxy_radicals"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/KMP2/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/UKGJEWEU/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::UKGJEWEU";
        dc:date                "2015-01-07 16:23:38.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::UKGJEWEU";
        dc:replaces            <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N102/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV15A1/>;
        pav:authoredOn         "2015-01-07 16:23:38.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/UKGJEWEU/2/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/UKGJEWEU/1/>;
        pav:version            "2";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/atmosphere_mass_content_of_sulfate_dry_aerosol_particles_expressed_as_sulfur/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/atmosphere_mass_content_of_sulfate_dry_aerosol_particles_expressed_as_sulfur>;
        owl:versionInfo        "2";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "\"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area. The \"atmosphere content\" of a quantity refers to the vertical integral from the surface to the top of the atmosphere. For the content between specified levels in the atmosphere, standard names including content_of_atmosphere_layer are used. The phrase \"expressed_as\" is used in the construction A_expressed_as_B, where B is a chemical constituent of A. It means that the quantity indicated by the standard name is calculated solely with respect to the B contained in A, neglecting all other chemical constituents of A. \"Aerosol\" means the system of suspended liquid or solid particles in air (except cloud droplets) and their carrier gas, the air itself. Aerosol particles take up ambient water (a process known as hygroscopic growth) depending on the relative humidity and the composition of the particles. \"Dry aerosol particles\" means aerosol particles without any water uptake. The chemical formula for the sulfate anion is SO4(2-)."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::UKGJEWEU";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "atmosphere_mass_content_of_sulfate_dry_aerosol_particles_expressed_as_sulfur"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/KMP2/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV15A1/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CFV15A1";
        dc:date                "2015-01-07 15:23:08.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CFV15A1";
        dc:isReplacedBy        <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/UKGJEWEU/>;
        pav:authoredOn         "2015-01-07 15:23:08.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV15A1/2/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV15A1/1/>;
        pav:version            "2";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "true";
        owl:sameAs             <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/atmosphere_mass_content_of_sulfate_dry_aerosol_expressed_as_sulfur> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/atmosphere_mass_content_of_sulfate_dry_aerosol_expressed_as_sulfur/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N102/>;
        owl:versionInfo        "2";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P04/current/G111/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P02/current/SUAT/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P64/current/G111/>;
        skos:definition        "\"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area.  The \"atmosphere content\" of a quantity refers to the vertical integral from the surface to the top of the atmosphere. For the content between specified levels in the atmosphere, standard names including content_of_atmosphere_layer are used.  The phrase 'expressed_as' is used in the construction A_expressed_as_B, where B is a chemical constituent of A. It means that the quantity indicated by the standard name is calculated solely with respect to the B contained in A, neglecting all other chemical constituents of A. \"Aerosol\" means the suspended liquid or solid particles in air (except cloud droplets).  Aerosol takes up ambient water (a process known as hygroscopic growth) depending on the relative humidity and the composition of the aerosol. \"Dry aerosol\" means aerosol without water. The chemical formula for the sulfate anion is SO4(2-)."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CFV15A1";
        skos:note              "deprecated"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "atmosphere_mass_content_of_sulfate_dry_aerosol_expressed_as_sulfur"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/KMP2/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N102/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CF12N102";
        dc:date                "2010-07-26 09:53:35.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CF12N102";
        dc:isReplacedBy        <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/UKGJEWEU/>;
        pav:authoredOn         "2010-07-26 09:53:35.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N102/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "true";
        owl:sameAs             <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/atmosphere_mass_content_of_sulfate_expressed_as_sulfur_dry_aerosol> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/atmosphere_mass_content_of_sulfate_expressed_as_sulfur_dry_aerosol/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV15A1/>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P04/current/G111/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P02/current/SUAT/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P64/current/G111/>;
        skos:definition        "\"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area.  The \"atmosphere content\" of a quantity refers to the vertical integral from the surface to the top of the atmosphere. For the content between specified levels in the atmosphere, standard names including content_of_atmosphere_layer are used.  \"Aerosol\" means the suspended liquid or solid particles in air (except cloud droplets).  Aerosol takes up ambient water (a process known as hygroscopic growth) depending on the relative humidity and the composition of the aerosol. \"Dry aerosol\" means aerosol without water. The phrase 'expressed_as' is used in the construction A_expressed_as_B, where B is a chemical constituent of A. It means that the quantity indicated by the standard name is calculated solely with respect to the B contained in A, neglecting all other chemical constituents of A."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CF12N102";
        skos:note              "deprecated"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "atmosphere_mass_content_of_sulfate_expressed_as_sulfur_dry_aerosol"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/KMP2/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0502/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CFSN0502";
        dc:date                "2006-09-26 18:12:43.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CFSN0502";
        pav:authoredOn         "2006-09-26 18:12:43.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0502/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/northward_atmosphere_heat_transport/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/northward_atmosphere_heat_transport>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "'Northward' indicates a vector component which is positive when directed northward (negative southward). 'Atmosphere heat transport' means total heat transport by the atmosphere by all processes."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CFSN0502";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "northward_atmosphere_heat_transport"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/WATT/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/GACJJFFJ/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::GACJJFFJ";
        dc:date                "2024-09-04 12:51:23.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::GACJJFFJ";
        pav:authoredOn         "2024-09-04 12:51:23.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/GACJJFFJ/3/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/GACJJFFJ/2/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/GACJJFFJ/1/>;
        pav:version            "3";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/burned_area_fraction/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/burned_area_fraction>;
        owl:versionInfo        "3";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P02/current/HBCH/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P02/current/LVEG/>;
        skos:definition        "\"Area fraction\" is the fraction of a grid cell's horizontal area that has some characteristic of interest. It is evaluated as the area of interest divided by the grid cell area, or if the cell_methods restricts the evaluation to some portion of that grid cell (e.g. \"where sea_ice\"), then it is the area of interest divided by the area of the identified portion. It may be expressed as a fraction, a percentage, or any other dimensionless representation of a fraction. \"Burned area\" means the area of burned vegetation."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::GACJJFFJ";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "burned_area_fraction"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/UUUU/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0233/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CFSN0233";
        dc:date                "2008-11-11 15:25:45.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CFSN0233";
        dc:isReplacedBy        <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0232/>;
        pav:authoredOn         "2008-11-11 15:25:45.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0233/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "true";
        owl:sameAs             <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/surface_upward_sensible_heat_flux_where_sea> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/surface_upward_sensible_heat_flux_where_sea/>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P02/current/HFLX/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P04/current/G204/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P64/current/G204/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0232/>;
        skos:definition        "The surface called 'surface' means the lower boundary of the atmosphere. Unless indicated, a quantity is assumed to apply to the whole area of each horizontal grid box. The qualifier where_type specifies instead that the quantity applies only to the part of the grid box of the named type. 'Upward' indicates a vector component which is positive when directed upward (negative downward). The surface sensible heat flux, also called 'turbulent' heat flux, is the exchange of heat between the surface and the air by motion of air. In accordance with common usage in geophysical disciplines, 'flux' implies per unit area, called 'flux density' in physics."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CFSN0233";
        skos:note              "deprecated"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "surface_upward_sensible_heat_flux_where_sea"@en .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0232/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CFSN0232";
        dc:date                "2006-09-26 18:12:43.0";
