<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/JCGDJQJ5/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::JCGDJQJ5";
        dc:date                "2018-06-11 18:10:05.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::JCGDJQJ5";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-06-11 18:10:05.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/JCGDJQJ5/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/surface_net_downward_longwave_dust_ambient_aerosol_particles_direct_radiative_effect/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/surface_net_downward_longwave_dust_ambient_aerosol_particles_direct_radiative_effect>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The surface called \"surface\" means the lower boundary of the atmosphere. \"Downward\" indicates a vector component which is positive when directed downward (negative upward). Net downward radiation is the difference between radiation from above (downwelling) and radiation from below (upwelling). The term \"longwave\" means longwave radiation. \"X_direct_radiative_effect\" refers to the instantaneous radiative impact of X on the Earth's energy balance, excluding secondary effects such as changes in cloud cover which may be caused by X. \"Aerosol\" means the system of suspended liquid or solid particles in air (except cloud droplets) and their carrier gas, the air itself. \"Ambient_aerosol\" means that the aerosol is measured or modelled at the ambient state of pressure, temperature and relative humidity that exists in its immediate environment. \"Ambient aerosol particles\" are aerosol particles that have taken up ambient water through hygroscopic growth. The extent of hygroscopic growth depends on the relative humidity and the composition of the particles. To specify the relative humidity and temperature at which the quantity described by the standard name applies, provide scalar coordinate variables with standard names of \"relative_humidity\" and \"air_temperature\"."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::JCGDJQJ5";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "surface_net_downward_longwave_dust_ambient_aerosol_particles_direct_radiative_effect"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/UFAA/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/8K77SAOV/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::8K77SAOV";
        dc:date                "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::8K77SAOV";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/8K77SAOV/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_254mEs_in_air/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_254mEs_in_air>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The phrase \"integral_wrt_X_of_Y\" means int Y dX. The data variable should have an axis for X specifying the limits of the integral as bounds. The phrase \"wrt\" means \"with respect to\". \"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Radioactivity concentration\" means radioactivity per unit volume of the medium. \"Es\" means the element \"einsteinium\" and \"254mEs\" is the metastable state of the isotope \"einsteinium-254\" with a half-life of 1.63e+00 days."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::8K77SAOV";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_254mEs_in_air"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/BSM3/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV15A32/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CFV15A32";
        dc:date                "2010-07-26 09:49:03.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CFV15A32";
