        skos:definition        "Mole fraction is used in the construction mole_fraction_of_X_in_Y, where X is a material constituent of Y.  The chemical formula of hydrogen bromide is HBr."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CFV8N32";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "mole_fraction_of_hydrogen_bromide_in_air"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/UUUU/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0284/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CFSN0284";
        dc:date                "2018-07-03 16:09:23.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CFSN0284";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-07-03 16:09:23.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0284/3/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0284/1/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0284/2/>;
        pav:version            "3";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/surface_downwelling_photosynthetic_photon_flux_in_air> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/surface_downwelling_photosynthetic_photon_flux_in_air/>;
        owl:versionInfo        "3";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P04/current/G436/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P02/current/VSRA/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P04/current/G210/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P64/current/G210/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P64/current/G436/>;
        skos:definition        "The surface called \"surface\" means the lower boundary of the atmosphere. Downwelling radiation is radiation from above. It does not mean \"net downward\". The sign convention is that \"upwelling\" is positive upwards and \"downwelling\" is positive downwards. \"Photosynthetic\" radiation is the part of the spectrum which is used in photosynthesis e.g. 400-700 nm. The range of wavelengths could be specified precisely by the bounds of a coordinate of radiation_wavelength. A photon flux is specified in terms of numbers of photons expressed in moles. In accordance with common usage in geophysical disciplines, \"flux\" implies per unit area, called \"flux density\" in physics."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CFSN0284";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "surface_downwelling_photosynthetic_photon_flux_in_air"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/M2MS/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV13N22/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CFV13N22";
        dc:date                "2021-09-20 14:41:46.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CFV13N22";
        pav:authoredOn         "2021-09-20 14:41:46.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV13N22/3/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV13N22/1/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV13N22/2/>;
        pav:version            "3";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/spell_length_of_days_with_air_temperature_above_threshold/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/spell_length_of_days_with_air_temperature_above_threshold>;
        owl:versionInfo        "3";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "Air temperature is the bulk temperature of the air, not the surface (skin) temperature. A spell is the number of consecutive days on which the condition X_below|above_threshold is satisfied. A variable whose standard name has the form spell_length_of_days_with_X_below|above_threshold must have a coordinate variable or scalar coordinate variable with the standard name of X to supply the threshold(s). It must have a climatological time variable, and a cell_method entry for within days which describes the processing of quantity X before the threshold is applied. A spell_length_of_days is an intensive quantity in time, and the cell_methods entry for over days can be any of the methods listed in Appendix E appropriate for intensive quantities e.g. \"maximum\", \"minimum\" or \"mean\"."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CFV13N22";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "spell_length_of_days_with_air_temperature_above_threshold"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/UTAA/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/Q6U0ADIH/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::Q6U0ADIH";
        dc:date                "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::Q6U0ADIH";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/Q6U0ADIH/1/>;
