<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/XOSJUTHH/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::XOSJUTHH";
        dc:date                "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::XOSJUTHH";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/XOSJUTHH/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/radioactivity_concentration_of_234mPa_in_air/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/radioactivity_concentration_of_234mPa_in_air>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "\"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Radioactivity concentration\" means radioactivity per unit volume of the medium. \"Pa\" means the element \"protactinium\" and \"234mPa\" is the metastable state of the isotope \"protactinium-234\" with a half-life of 8.13e-04 days."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::XOSJUTHH";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "radioactivity_concentration_of_234mPa_in_air"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/BQM3/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N290/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CF12N290";
        dc:date                "2009-07-06 15:41:29.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CF12N290";
        pav:authoredOn         "2009-07-06 15:41:29.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N290/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/mass_concentration_of_molecular_hydrogen_in_air/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/mass_concentration_of_molecular_hydrogen_in_air>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "Mass concentration means mass per unit volume and is used in the construction mass_concentration_of_X_in_Y, where X is a material constituent of Y.  A chemical species denoted by X may be described by a single term such as 'nitrogen' or a phrase such as 'nox_expressed_as_nitrogen'. The chemical formula for molecular hydrogen is H2."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CF12N290";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "mass_concentration_of_molecular_hydrogen_in_air"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/UKMC/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/55KUDP8X/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::55KUDP8X";
        dc:date                "2019-06-17 13:47:18.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::55KUDP8X";
        pav:authoredOn         "2019-06-17 13:47:18.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/55KUDP8X/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0436/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/product_of_northward_wind_and_lagrangian_tendency_of_air_pressure/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/product_of_northward_wind_and_lagrangian_tendency_of_air_pressure>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The phrase \"product_of_X_and_Y\" means X*Y. \"Northward\" indicates a vector component which is positive when directed northward (negative southward). Wind is defined as a two-dimensional (horizontal) air velocity vector, with no vertical component. (Vertical motion in the atmosphere has the standard name upward_air_velocity.) The phrase \"tendency_of_X\" means derivative of X with respect to time. The Lagrangian tendency of a quantity is its rate of change following the motion of the fluid, also called the \"material derivative\" or \"convective derivative\". The Lagrangian tendency of air pressure, often called \"omega\", plays the role of the upward component of air velocity when air pressure is being used as the vertical coordinate. If the vertical air velocity is upwards, it is negative when expressed as a tendency of air pressure; downwards is positive. Air pressure is the force per unit area which would be exerted when the moving gas molecules of which the air is composed strike a theoretical surface of any orientation."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::55KUDP8X";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "product_of_northward_wind_and_lagrangian_tendency_of_air_pressure"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/PAM2/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0436/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CFSN0436";
        dc:date                "2019-06-17 13:47:19.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CFSN0436";
        pav:authoredOn         "2019-06-17 13:47:19.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0436/2/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0436/1/>;
        pav:version            "2";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "true";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/product_of_northward_wind_and_omega/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/55KUDP8X/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/product_of_northward_wind_and_omega>;
        owl:versionInfo        "2";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "'product_of_X_and_Y' means X*Y. 'Northward' indicates a vector component which is positive when directed northward (negative southward). Wind is defined as a two-dimensional (horizontal) air velocity vector, with no vertical component. (Vertical motion in the atmosphere has the standard name upward_air_velocity.) 'omegaX' is used for brevity to mean 'lagrangian_tendency_of_air_pressure in standard names constructed as a combination of omega with some other quantity."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CFSN0436";
        skos:note              "deprecated"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "product_of_northward_wind_and_omega"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/PAM2/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N38/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CF12N38";
        dc:date                "2009-07-06 15:41:29.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CF12N38";
        pav:authoredOn         "2009-07-06 15:41:29.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N38/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/atmosphere_mass_content_of_dinitrogen_pentoxide> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/atmosphere_mass_content_of_dinitrogen_pentoxide/>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P02/current/AAMN/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P04/current/G161/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P04/current/G156/>;
        skos:definition        "\"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area.  The \"atmosphere content\" of a quantity refers to the vertical integral from the surface to the top of the atmosphere. For the content between specified levels in the atmosphere, standard names including content_of_atmosphere_layer are used.  The chemical formula for dinitrogen pentoxide is N2O5."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CF12N38";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "atmosphere_mass_content_of_dinitrogen_pentoxide"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/KMP2/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/OJUDV53W/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::OJUDV53W";
        dc:date                "2023-04-24 17:39:19.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::OJUDV53W";
        pav:authoredOn         "2023-04-24 17:39:19.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/OJUDV53W/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/ratio_of_volume_extinction_coefficient_to_volume_backwards_scattering_coefficient_by_ranging_instrument_in_air_due_to_ambient_aerosol_particles/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/ratio_of_volume_extinction_coefficient_to_volume_backwards_scattering_coefficient_by_ranging_instrument_in_air_due_to_ambient_aerosol_particles>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The ratio of volume extinction coefficient to volume backwards scattering coefficient by ranging instrument in air due to ambient aerosol particles (often called \"lidar ratio\") is the ratio of the \"volume extinction coefficient\" and the \"volume backwards scattering coefficient of radiative flux by ranging instrument in air due to ambient aerosol particles\". The ratio is assumed to be related to the same wavelength of incident radiation. \"Ambient_aerosol\" means that the aerosol is measured or modelled at the ambient state of pressure, temperature and relative humidity that exists in its immediate environment. \"Ambient aerosol particles\" are aerosol particles that have taken up ambient water through hygroscopic growth. The extent of hygroscopic growth depends on the relative humidity and the composition of the particles. The specification of a physical process by the phrase \"due_to_\" process means that the quantity named is a single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity named by omitting the phrase."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::OJUDV53W";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "ratio_of_volume_extinction_coefficient_to_volume_backwards_scattering_coefficient_by_ranging_instrument_in_air_due_to_ambient_aerosol_particles"@en .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N349/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CF12N349";
        dc:date                "2019-05-14 17:27:19.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CF12N349";
        pav:authoredOn         "2019-05-14 17:27:19.0";
