<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/AFZN3MEY/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::AFZN3MEY";
        dc:date                "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::AFZN3MEY";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/AFZN3MEY/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/surface_radioactivity_content_of_135I/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/surface_radioactivity_content_of_135I>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The surface called \"surface\" means the lower boundary of the atmosphere. \"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area. \"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"I\" means the element \"iodine\" and \"135I\" is the isotope \"iodine-135\" with a half-life of 2.79e-01 days."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::AFZN3MEY";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "surface_radioactivity_content_of_135I"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/BQSM/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/GIWUWAF2/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::GIWUWAF2";
        dc:date                "2026-06-08 13:55:32.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::GIWUWAF2";
        pav:authoredOn         "2026-06-08 13:55:32.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/GIWUWAF2/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/mole_flux_of_nitrogen_out_of_sea_floor_sediment_due_to_denitrification/>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "In accordance with common usage in geophysical disciplines, \"flux\" implies per unit area, called \"flux density\" in physics. The surface called \"sea floor\" means the lower boundary of the ocean. \"Sea floor sediment\" is sediment deposited at the sea bed. The specification of a physical process by the phrase \"due_to_\" process means that the quantity named is a single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity named by omitting the phrase. \"Denitrification\" is the conversion of nitrate into gaseous compounds such as nitric oxide, nitrous oxide and molecular nitrogen which are then emitted to the atmosphere."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::GIWUWAF2";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "mole_flux_of_nitrogen_out_of_sea_floor_sediment_due_to_denitrification"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/M2MS/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N303/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CF12N303";
        dc:date                "2009-07-06 15:41:29.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CF12N303";
        pav:authoredOn         "2009-07-06 15:41:29.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N303/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/mass_concentration_of_organic_detritus_expressed_as_nitrogen_in_sea_water> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/mass_concentration_of_organic_detritus_expressed_as_nitrogen_in_sea_water/>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P02/current/EXUV/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P64/current/G901/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P04/current/G901/>;
        skos:definition        "Mass concentration means mass per unit volume and is used in the construction mass_concentration_of_X_in_Y, where X is a material constituent of Y.  A chemical species denoted by X may be described by a single term such as 'nitrogen' or a phrase such as 'nox_expressed_as_nitrogen'. The phrase 'expressed_as' is used in the construction A_expressed_as_B, where B is a chemical constituent of A. It means that the quantity indicated by the standard name is calculated solely with respect to the B contained in A, neglecting all other chemical constituents of A. Organic detritus are particles of debris from decaying plants and animals."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CF12N303";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "mass_concentration_of_organic_detritus_expressed_as_nitrogen_in_sea_water"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/UKMC/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/77HZPQ9W/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::77HZPQ9W";
        dc:date                "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::77HZPQ9W";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/77HZPQ9W/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/surface_radioactivity_content_of_83Se/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/surface_radioactivity_content_of_83Se>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The surface called \"surface\" means the lower boundary of the atmosphere. \"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area. \"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Se\" means the element \"selenium\" and \"83Se\" is the isotope \"selenium-83\" with a half-life of 1.56e-02 days."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::77HZPQ9W";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "surface_radioactivity_content_of_83Se"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/BQSM/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/HAAAACAH/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::HAAAACAH";
        dc:date                "2012-09-19 14:08:40.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::HAAAACAH";
        pav:authoredOn         "2012-09-19 14:08:40.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/HAAAACAH/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/tendency_of_atmosphere_mass_content_of_pentane_due_to_emission_from_waste_treatment_and_disposal/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/tendency_of_atmosphere_mass_content_of_pentane_due_to_emission_from_waste_treatment_and_disposal>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P02/current/AALK/>;
        skos:definition        "\"tendency_of_X\" means derivative of X with respect to time. \"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area. The \"atmosphere content\" of a quantity refers to the vertical integral from the surface to the top of the atmosphere. For the content between specified levels in the atmosphere, standard names including \"content_of_atmosphere_layer\" are used. The mass is the total mass of the molecules. The specification of a physical process by the phrase \"due_to_\" process means that the quantity named is a single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity named by omitting the phrase. \"Emission\" means emission from a primary source located anywhere within the atmosphere, including at the lower boundary (i.e. earth&amp;apos;s surface). \"Emission\" is a process entirely distinct from \"re-emission\" which is used in some standard names. The chemical formula for pentane is C5H12. Pentane is a member of the group of hydrocarbons known as alkanes. There are standard names for the alkane group as well as for some of the individual species. The \"waste treatment and disposal\" sector comprises solid waste disposal on land, wastewater handling, waste incineration and other waste disposal. \"Waste treatment and disposal\" is the term used in standard names to describe a collection of emission sources. A variable which has this value for the standard_name attribute should be accompanied by a comment attribute which lists the source categories and provides a reference to the categorization scheme, for example, \"IPCC (Intergovernmental Panel on Climate Change) source categories 6A, 6B, 6C and 6D as defined in the 2006 IPCC guidelines for national greenhouse gas inventories\"."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::HAAAACAH";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "tendency_of_atmosphere_mass_content_of_pentane_due_to_emission_from_waste_treatment_and_disposal"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/KSP2/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/4O9B7F67/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
