        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_135mCs_in_air/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_135mCs_in_air>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The phrase \"integral_wrt_X_of_Y\" means int Y dX. The data variable should have an axis for X specifying the limits of the integral as bounds. The phrase \"wrt\" means \"with respect to\". \"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Radioactivity concentration\" means radioactivity per unit volume of the medium. \"Cs\" means the element \"cesium\" and \"135mCs\" is the metastable state of the isotope \"cesium-135\" with a half-life of 3.68e-02 days."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::4M2P1FWD";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_135mCs_in_air"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/BSM3/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0001/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CFSN0001";
        dc:date                "2024-09-04 12:51:23.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CFSN0001";
        pav:authoredOn         "2024-09-04 12:51:23.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0001/5/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0001/2/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0001/4/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0001/1/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0001/3/>;
        pav:version            "5";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/area_fraction/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/area_fraction>;
        owl:versionInfo        "5";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "\"Area fraction\" is the fraction of a grid cell's horizontal area that has some characteristic of interest. It is evaluated as the area of interest divided by the grid cell area, or if the cell_methods restricts the evaluation to some portion of that grid cell (e.g. \"where sea_ice\"), then it is the area of interest divided by the area of the identified portion. It may be expressed as a fraction, a percentage, or any other dimensionless representation of a fraction. To specify which area is quantified by a variable with standard name area_fraction, provide a coordinate variable or scalar coordinate variable with standard name area_type. Alternatively, if one is defined, use a more specific standard name of X_area_fraction for the fraction of horizontal area occupied by X."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CFSN0001";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "area_fraction"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/UUUU/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV13N42/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CFV13N42";
        dc:date                "2010-03-11 14:38:28.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CFV13N42";
