        skos:definition        "\"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Radioactivity concentration\" means radioactivity per unit volume of the medium. \"Te\" means the element \"tellurium\" and \"125mTe\" is the metastable state of the isotope \"tellurium-125\" with a half-life of 5.81e+01 days."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::GQK3MVKN";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
