        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The surface called \"surface\" means the lower boundary of the atmosphere. \"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area. \"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Pr\" means the element \"praseodymium\" and \"142mPr\" is the metastable state of the isotope \"praseodymium-142\" with a half-life of 1.01e-02 days."@en;
