<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/7YP3AA62/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::7YP3AA62";
        dc:date                "2017-06-26 15:24:29.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::7YP3AA62";
        pav:authoredOn         "2017-06-26 15:24:29.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/7YP3AA62/3/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/7YP3AA62/2/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/7YP3AA62/1/>;
        pav:version            "3";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/mass_fraction_of_pm2p5_ammonium_dry_aerosol_particles_in_air/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/mass_fraction_of_pm2p5_ammonium_dry_aerosol_particles_in_air>;
        owl:versionInfo        "3";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "Mass fraction is used in the construction \"mass_fraction_of_X_in_Y\", where X is a material constituent of Y. It means the ratio of the mass of X to the mass of Y (including X). A chemical species denoted by X may be described by a single term such as \"nitrogen\" or a phrase such as \"nox_expressed_as_nitrogen\". \"Aerosol\" means the system of suspended liquid or solid particles in air (except cloud droplets) and their carrier gas, the air itself. Aerosol particles take up ambient water (a process known as hygroscopic growth) depending on the relative humidity and the composition of the particles. \"Dry aerosol particles\" means aerosol particles without any water uptake. \"Pm2p5 aerosol\" means atmospheric particulate compounds with an aerodynamic diameter of less than or equal to 2.5 micrometers. The chemical formula for ammonium is NH4."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::7YP3AA62";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "mass_fraction_of_pm2p5_ammonium_dry_aerosol_particles_in_air"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/UUUU/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N24/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CF12N24";
        dc:date                "2009-07-06 15:41:29.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CF12N24";
        pav:authoredOn         "2009-07-06 15:41:29.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N24/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/atmosphere_mass_content_of_carbon_monoxide> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/atmosphere_mass_content_of_carbon_monoxide/>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P02/current/ACO2/> , <http://rdfdata.eionet.europa.eu/airquality/components/10> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P04/current/G133/>;
        skos:definition        "\"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area.  The \"atmosphere content\" of a quantity refers to the vertical integral from the surface to the top of the atmosphere. For the content between specified levels in the atmosphere, standard names including content_of_atmosphere_layer are used.  The chemical formula of carbon monoxide is CO."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CF12N24";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "atmosphere_mass_content_of_carbon_monoxide"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/KMP2/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0400/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CFSN0400";
        dc:date                "2024-05-20 20:39:49.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CFSN0400";
        pav:authoredOn         "2024-05-20 20:39:49.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0400/2/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0400/1/>;
        pav:version            "2";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/product_of_upward_air_velocity_and_air_temperature/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/product_of_upward_air_velocity_and_air_temperature>;
        owl:versionInfo        "2";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The product \"product_of_X_and_Y\" means X*Y. Air temperature is the bulk temperature of the air, not the surface (skin) temperature. A velocity is a vector quantity. \"Upward\" indicates a vector component which is positive when directed upward (negative downward). Upward air velocity is the vertical component of the 3D air velocity vector. It is strongly recommended that a variable with this standard name should have a units_metadata attribute, with one of the values \"on-scale\" or \"difference\", whichever is appropriate for the data, because it is essential to know whether the temperature is on-scale (meaning relative to the origin of the scale indicated by the units) or refers to temperature differences (implying that the origin of the temperature scale is irrevelant), in order to convert the units correctly (cf. https://cfconventions.org/cf-conventions/cf-conventions.html#temperature-units)."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CFSN0400";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "product_of_upward_air_velocity_and_air_temperature"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/KMTS/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/51Z644TH/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::51Z644TH";
        dc:date                "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::51Z644TH";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/51Z644TH/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_102mTc_in_air/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_102mTc_in_air>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The phrase \"integral_wrt_X_of_Y\" means int Y dX. The data variable should have an axis for X specifying the limits of the integral as bounds. The phrase \"wrt\" means \"with respect to\". \"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Radioactivity concentration\" means radioactivity per unit volume of the medium. \"Tc\" means the element \"technetium\" and \"102mTc\" is the metastable state of the isotope \"technetium-102\" with a half-life of 2.98e-03 days."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::51Z644TH";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_102mTc_in_air"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/BSM3/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CTC0295V/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CTC0295V";
        dc:date                "2013-11-08 14:08:46.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CTC0295V";
        pav:authoredOn         "2013-11-08 14:08:46.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CTC0295V/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/atmosphere_lifting_condensation_level/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/atmosphere_lifting_condensation_level>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The lifting condensation level is the height at which the relative humidity of an air parcel cooled by dry adiabatic lifting would reach 100%. A coordinate variable of original_air_pressure_of_lifted_parcel should be specified to indicate the starting height of the lifted parcel."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CTC0295V";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "atmosphere_lifting_condensation_level"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/ULAA/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0634/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CFSN0634";
        dc:date                "2006-09-26 18:12:43.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CFSN0634";
        pav:authoredOn         "2006-09-26 18:12:43.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0634/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/grid_latitude/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/grid_latitude>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P02/current/ALAT/>;
        skos:definition        "Latitude is positive northward; its units of degree_north (or equivalent) indicate this explicitly. In a latitude-longitude system defined with respect to a rotated North Pole, the standard name of grid_latitude should be used instead of latitude. Grid latitude is positive in the grid-northward direction, but its units should be plain degree."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CFSN0634";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "grid_latitude"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/UAAA/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N20/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CF12N20";
        dc:date                "2009-07-06 15:41:29.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CF12N20";
        pav:authoredOn         "2009-07-06 15:41:29.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N20/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/atmosphere_mass_content_of_bromine_nitrate/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/atmosphere_mass_content_of_bromine_nitrate>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P02/current/AAMN/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P02/current/HLAT/>;
        skos:definition        "\"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area.  The \"atmosphere content\" of a quantity refers to the vertical integral from the surface to the top of the atmosphere. For the content between specified levels in the atmosphere, standard names including content_of_atmosphere_layer are used.  The chemical formula for bromine nitrate is BrONO2. The chemical formula for the nitrate anion is NO3-."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CF12N20";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "atmosphere_mass_content_of_bromine_nitrate"@en;
