        skos:definition        "The surface called \"surface\" means the lower boundary of the atmosphere. \"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area. \"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Ag\" means the element \"silver\" and \"113mAg\" is the metastable state of the isotope \"silver-113\" with a half-life of 7.64e-04 days."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::U2SI4T3U";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "surface_radioactivity_content_of_113mAg"@en;
