        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The surface called \"surface\" means the lower boundary of the atmosphere. \"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area. \"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Pa\" means the element \"protactinium\" and \"231Pa\" is the isotope \"protactinium-231\" with a half-life of 1.19e+07 days."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::ARXW0V2G";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "surface_radioactivity_content_of_231Pa"@en;
