        skos:definition        "The construction \"atmosphere_moles_of_X\" means the total number of moles of X in the entire atmosphere, i.e. summed over the atmospheric column and over the entire globe. The chemical formula for HCFC141b is CH3CCl2F. The IUPAC name for HCFC141b is 1,1-dichloro-1-fluoroethane."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CF12N143";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "atmosphere_moles_of_hcfc141b"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/MOLE/> .

