<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N352/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CF12N352";
        dc:date                "2019-05-14 17:27:19.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CF12N352";
        pav:authoredOn         "2019-05-14 17:27:19.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N352/3/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N352/1/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N352/2/>;
        pav:version            "3";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/mass_fraction_of_cfc114_in_air/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/mass_fraction_of_cfc114_in_air>;
        owl:versionInfo        "3";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P02/current/HLAT/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P04/current/G146/>;
        skos:definition        "\"Mass fraction\" is used in the construction \"mass_fraction_of_X_in_Y\", where X is a material constituent of Y. It means the ratio of the mass of X to the mass of Y (including X). A chemical or biological species denoted by X may be described by a single term such as \"nitrogen\" or a phrase such as \"nox_expressed_as_nitrogen\". The chemical formula of CFC114 is CClF2CClF2. The IUPAC name for CFC114 is 1,2-dichloro-1,1,2,2-tetrafluoroethane."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CF12N352";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "mass_fraction_of_cfc114_in_air"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/UUUU/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N312/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CF12N312";
        dc:date                "2015-01-07 15:23:06.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CF12N312";
        dc:isReplacedBy        <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/FQM4CFXQ/>;
        pav:authoredOn         "2015-01-07 15:23:06.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N312/2/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N312/1/>;
        pav:version            "2";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "true";
        owl:sameAs             <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/mass_concentration_of_primary_particulate_organic_matter_dry_aerosol_in_air> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/mass_concentration_of_primary_particulate_organic_matter_dry_aerosol_in_air/>;
        owl:versionInfo        "2";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P02/current/AORG/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P64/current/H316/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P04/current/H316/>;
        skos:definition        "Mass concentration means mass per unit volume and is used in the construction mass_concentration_of_X_in_Y, where X is a material constituent of Y.  A chemical species denoted by X may be described by a single term such as 'nitrogen' or a phrase such as 'nox_expressed_as_nitrogen'. \"Aerosol\" means the suspended liquid or solid particles in air (except cloud droplets).  Aerosol takes up ambient water (a process known as hygroscopic growth) depending on the relative humidity and the composition of the aerosol. \"Dry aerosol\" means aerosol without water. \"Primary particulate organic matter \" means all organic matter emitted directly to the atmosphere as particles except black carbon. The sum of primary_particulate_organic_matter_dry_aerosol and secondary_particulate_organic_matter_dry_aerosol is particulate_organic_matter_dry_aerosol."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CF12N312";
        skos:note              "deprecated"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "mass_concentration_of_primary_particulate_organic_matter_dry_aerosol_in_air"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/UKMC/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/FQM4CFXQ/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::FQM4CFXQ";
        dc:date                "2015-01-07 16:23:38.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::FQM4CFXQ";
        dc:replaces            <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N312/>;
        pav:authoredOn         "2015-01-07 16:23:38.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/FQM4CFXQ/2/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/FQM4CFXQ/1/>;
        pav:version            "2";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/mass_concentration_of_primary_particulate_organic_matter_dry_aerosol_particles_in_air/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/mass_concentration_of_primary_particulate_organic_matter_dry_aerosol_particles_in_air>;
        owl:versionInfo        "2";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "Mass concentration means mass per unit volume and is used in the construction mass_concentration_of_X_in_Y, where X is a material constituent of Y. A chemical species denoted by X may be described by a single term such as \"nitrogen\" or a phrase such as \"nox_expressed_as_nitrogen\". \"Aerosol\" means the system of suspended liquid or solid particles in air (except cloud droplets) and their carrier gas, the air itself. Aerosol takes up ambient water (a process known as hygroscopic growth) depending on the relative humidity and the composition of the aerosol. \"Dry aerosol particles\" means aerosol particles without any water uptake. \"Primary particulate organic matter \" means all organic matter emitted directly to the atmosphere as particles except elemental carbon. The sum of primary_particulate_organic_matter_dry_aerosol and secondary_particulate_organic_matter_dry_aerosol is particulate_organic_matter_dry_aerosol."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::FQM4CFXQ";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "mass_concentration_of_primary_particulate_organic_matter_dry_aerosol_particles_in_air"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/UKMC/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0401/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CFSN0401";
        dc:date                "2006-09-26 18:12:43.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CFSN0401";
        pav:authoredOn         "2006-09-26 18:12:43.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0401/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/product_of_upward_air_velocity_and_specific_humidity/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/product_of_upward_air_velocity_and_specific_humidity>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "'product_of_X_and_Y' means X*Y. 'specific' means per unit mass. A velocity is a vector quantity. 'Upward' indicates a vector component which is positive when directed upward (negative downward). Specific humidity is the mass fraction of water vapor in (moist) air. Upward air velocity is the vertical component of the 3D air velocity vector."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CFSN0401";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "product_of_upward_air_velocity_and_specific_humidity"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/UVAA/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF14N22/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CF14N22";
        dc:date                "2018-12-17 17:17:12.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CF14N22";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-12-17 17:17:12.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF14N22/2/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF14N22/1/>;
        pav:version            "2";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/mole_concentration_of_calcite_expressed_as_carbon_in_sea_water_at_saturation/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/mole_concentration_of_calcite_expressed_as_carbon_in_sea_water_at_saturation>;
        owl:versionInfo        "2";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P02/current/CING/>;
        skos:definition        "Mole concentration means number of moles per unit volume, also called \"molarity\", and is used in the construction mole_concentration_of_X_in_Y, where X is a material constituent of Y. A chemical or biological species denoted by X may be described by a single term such as \"nitrogen\" or a phrase such as \"nox_expressed_as_nitrogen\". \"Mole concentration at saturation\" means the mole concentration in a saturated solution.The phrase \"expressed_as\" is used in the construction A_expressed_as_B, where B is a chemical constituent of A. It means that the quantity indicated by the standard name is calculated solely with respect to the B contained in A, neglecting all other chemical constituents of A. Calcite is a mineral that is a polymorph of calcium carbonate. The chemical formula of calcite is CaCO3. Standard names also exist for aragonite, another polymorph of calcium carbonate."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CF14N22";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "mole_concentration_of_calcite_expressed_as_carbon_in_sea_water_at_saturation"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/MLM3/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N578/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CF12N578";
        dc:date                "2018-05-29 16:57:01.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CF12N578";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-05-29 16:57:01.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N578/2/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N578/1/>;
        pav:version            "2";
