        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/atmosphere_moles_of_dichlorine_peroxide/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/atmosphere_moles_of_dichlorine_peroxide>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P02/current/HLAT/>;
        skos:definition        "The construction \"atmosphere_moles_of_X\" means the total number of moles of X in the entire atmosphere, i.e. summed over the atmospheric column and over the entire globe. The chemical formula for dichlorine peroxide is Cl2O2."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CF12N132";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "atmosphere_moles_of_dichlorine_peroxide"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/MOLE/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/VTPPM9AP/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::VTPPM9AP";
        dc:date                "2025-03-19 08:31:34.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::VTPPM9AP";
        pav:authoredOn         "2025-03-19 08:31:34.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/VTPPM9AP/2/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/VTPPM9AP/1/>;
        pav:version            "2";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "true";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/tendency_of_sea_water_salinity_expressed_as_salt_content_due_to_parameterized_mesoscale_eddy_diffusion/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/MVH1DRXB/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/tendency_of_sea_water_salinity_expressed_as_salt_content_due_to_parameterized_mesoscale_eddy_diffusion>;
        owl:versionInfo        "2";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The phrase \"tendency_of_X\" means derivative of X with respect to time. \"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area. The specification of a physical process by the phrase due_to_process means that the quantity named is a single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity named by omitting the phrase. Parameterized mesoscale eddy diffusive processes include diffusion along neutral directions in the interior of the ocean and horizontal diffusion in the surface boundary layer. The processes occur on a spatial scale of many tens of kilometres and an evolutionary time of weeks."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::VTPPM9AP";
        skos:note              "deprecated"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "tendency_of_sea_water_salinity_expressed_as_salt_content_due_to_parameterized_mesoscale_eddy_diffusion"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/KSP2/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/MVH1DRXB/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::MVH1DRXB";
        dc:date                "2025-03-19 08:31:34.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::MVH1DRXB";
        pav:authoredOn         "2025-03-19 08:31:34.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/MVH1DRXB/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/VTPPM9AP/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/tendency_of_integral_wrt_depth_of_sea_water_salinity_expressed_as_salt_mass_content_due_to_parameterized_mesoscale_eddy_diffusion/>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The phrase \"tendency_of_X\" means derivative of X with respect to time. The phrase \"integral_wrt_X_of_Y\" means int Y dX. To specify the limits of the integral the data variable should have an axis for X and associated coordinate bounds. If no axis for X is associated with the data variable, or no coordinate bounds are specified, it is assumed that the integral is calculated over the entire vertical extent of the medium, e.g, if the medium is air the integral is assumed to be calculated over the full depth of the atmosphere. The abbreviation \"wrt\" means \"with respect to\". Depth is the vertical distance below the surface. Sea water salinity is the salt concentration of sea water, often on the Practical Salinity Scale of 1978. However, the unqualified term 'salinity' is generic and does not necessarily imply any particular method of calculation. There are standard names for the more precisely defined salinity quantities sea_water_knudsen_salinity, S_K (used for salinity observations between 1901 and 1966), sea_water_cox_salinity, S_C (used for salinity observations between 1967 and 1977), sea_water_practical_salinity, S_P (used for salinity observations from 1978 to the present day), sea_water_absolute_salinity, S_A, sea_water_preformed_salinity, S_*, and sea_water_reference_salinity. Salinity quantities that do not match any of the precise definitions should be given the more general standard name of sea_water_salinity. Parameterized mesoscale eddy diffusive processes include diffusion along neutral directions in the interior of the ocean and horizontal diffusion in the surface boundary layer. The processes occur on a spatial scale of many tens of kilometres and an evolutionary time of weeks."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::MVH1DRXB";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "tendency_of_integral_wrt_depth_of_sea_water_salinity_expressed_as_salt_mass_content_due_to_parameterized_mesoscale_eddy_diffusion"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/KSP2/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/7GSG7WZD/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::7GSG7WZD";
        dc:date                "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::7GSG7WZD";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/7GSG7WZD/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_148mPm_in_air/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_148mPm_in_air>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The phrase \"integral_wrt_X_of_Y\" means int Y dX. The data variable should have an axis for X specifying the limits of the integral as bounds. The phrase \"wrt\" means \"with respect to\". \"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Radioactivity concentration\" means radioactivity per unit volume of the medium. \"Pm\" means the element \"promethium\" and \"148mPm\" is the metastable state of the isotope \"promethium-148\" with a half-life of 4.14e+01 days."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::7GSG7WZD";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_148mPm_in_air"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/BSM3/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0306/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CFSN0306";
        dc:date                "2006-09-26 18:12:43.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CFSN0306";
        pav:authoredOn         "2006-09-26 18:12:43.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0306/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/sound_intensity_level_in_water/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/sound_intensity_level_in_water>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "Sound intensity is the sound energy per unit time per unit area. Sound intensity level in water is expressed on a logarithmic scale with reference to a sound intensity of 6.7e-19 W m-2. LI = 10 log10(I/I0) where LI is sound intensity level, I is sound intensity and I0 is the reference sound intensity."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CFSN0306";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "sound_intensity_level_in_water"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/UDBL/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/PUHA3XB4/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::PUHA3XB4";
        dc:date                "2022-03-18 12:42:55.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::PUHA3XB4";
        pav:authoredOn         "2022-03-18 12:42:55.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/PUHA3XB4/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/mass_concentration_of_zeaxanthin_in_sea_water/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/mass_concentration_of_zeaxanthin_in_sea_water>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "\"Mass concentration\" means mass per unit volume and is used in the construction \"mass_concentration_of_X_in_Y\", where X is a material constituent of Y. A chemical species or biological group denoted by X may be described by a single term such as \"nitrogen\" or a phrase such as \"nox_expressed_as_nitrogen\". The chemical formula of zeaxanthin is C40H56O2. The equivalent term in the NERC P01 Parameter Usage Vocabulary may be found at http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P01/current/ZEAXXXXX/2/."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::PUHA3XB4";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "mass_concentration_of_zeaxanthin_in_sea_water"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/UKMC/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/BBAH2117/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::BBAH2117";
        dc:date                "2018-10-15 12:56:49.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::BBAH2117";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-10-15 12:56:49.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/BBAH2117/4/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/BBAH2117/2/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/BBAH2117/3/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/BBAH2117/1/>;
        pav:version            "4";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/platform_zenith_angle/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/platform_zenith_angle>;
        owl:versionInfo        "4";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P02/current/HEAD/>;
        skos:definition        "Platform zenith angle is the the angle between the line of sight to the platform and the local zenith at the observation target. This angle is measured starting from directly overhead and its range is from zero (directly overhead the observation target) to 180 degrees (directly below the observation target). Local zenith is a line perpendicular to the Earth's surface at a given location. \"Observation target\" means a location on the Earth defined by the sensor performing the observations. A standard name also exists for sensor_zenith_angle. For some viewing geometries the sensor and the platform cannot be assumed to be close enough to neglect the difference in calculated zenith angle. A \"platform\" is a structure or vehicle that serves as a base for mounting sensors. Platforms include, but are not limited to, satellites, aeroplanes, ships, buoys, instruments, ground stations, and masts."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::BBAH2117";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "platform_zenith_angle"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/UAAA/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/TAIG5Z2H/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::TAIG5Z2H";
        dc:date                "2025-03-19 08:31:36.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::TAIG5Z2H";
        pav:authoredOn         "2025-03-19 08:31:36.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/TAIG5Z2H/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/mole_concentration_of_nanophytoplankton_expressed_as_carbon_in_sea_water/>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "\"Mole concentration\" means number of moles per unit volume, also called \"molarity\", and is used in the construction \"mole_concentration_of_X_in_Y\", where X is a material constituent of Y. A chemical species or biological group denoted by X may be described by a single term such as \"nitrogen\" or a phrase such as \"nox_expressed_as_nitrogen\". The phrase \"expressed_as\" is used in the construction \"A_expressed_as_B\", where B is a chemical constituent of A. It means that the quantity indicated by the standard name is calculated solely with respect to the B contained in A, neglecting all other chemical constituents of A. Phytoplankton are algae that grow where there is sufficient light to support photosynthesis. Nanophytoplankton are phytoplankton in the size range 2 - 20 micrometers."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::TAIG5Z2H";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "mole_concentration_of_nanophytoplankton_expressed_as_carbon_in_sea_water"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/MLM3/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N475/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CF12N475";
        dc:date                "2019-03-04 17:29:46.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CF12N475";
        pav:authoredOn         "2019-03-04 17:29:46.0";
