<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/7ZU6EO7W/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::7ZU6EO7W";
        dc:date                "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::7ZU6EO7W";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/7ZU6EO7W/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_239Np_in_air/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_239Np_in_air>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The phrase \"integral_wrt_X_of_Y\" means int Y dX. The data variable should have an axis for X specifying the limits of the integral as bounds. The phrase \"wrt\" means \"with respect to\". \"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Radioactivity concentration\" means radioactivity per unit volume of the medium. \"Np\" means the element \"neptunium\" and \"239Np\" is the isotope \"neptunium-239\" with a half-life of 2.35e+00 days."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::7ZU6EO7W";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_239Np_in_air"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/BSM3/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF14N58/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CF14N58";
        dc:date                "2010-07-26 08:27:36.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CF14N58";
        pav:authoredOn         "2010-07-26 08:27:36.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF14N58/2/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF14N58/1/>;
        pav:version            "2";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/sinking_mole_flux_of_calcite_expressed_as_carbon_in_sea_water/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/sinking_mole_flux_of_calcite_expressed_as_carbon_in_sea_water>;
        owl:versionInfo        "2";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P02/current/TCFX/>;
        skos:definition        "The phrase 'expressed_as' is used in the construction A_expressed_as_B, where B is a chemical constituent of A. It means that the quantity indicated by the standard name is calculated solely with respect to the B contained in A, neglecting all other chemical constituents of A. In accordance with common usage in geophysical disciplines, \"flux\" implies per unit area, called \"flux density\" in physics.   'Sinking' is the gravitational settling of particulate matter suspended in a liquid. A sinking flux is positive downwards and is calculated relative to the movement of the surrounding fluid. Calcite is a mineral that is a polymorph of calcium carbonate. The chemical formula of calcite is CaCO3. Standard names also exist for aragonite, another polymorph of calcium carbonate."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CF14N58";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "sinking_mole_flux_of_calcite_expressed_as_carbon_in_sea_water"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/M2MS/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N48/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CF12N48";
        dc:date                "2019-05-14 17:27:19.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CF12N48";
        pav:authoredOn         "2019-05-14 17:27:19.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N48/3/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N48/2/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N48/1/>;
        pav:version            "3";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/atmosphere_mass_content_of_halon1202/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/atmosphere_mass_content_of_halon1202>;
        owl:versionInfo        "3";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P02/current/HLAT/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P04/current/G147/>;
        skos:definition        "\"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area. The \"atmosphere content\" of a quantity refers to the vertical integral from the surface to the top of the atmosphere. For the content between specified levels in the atmosphere, standard names including \"content_of_atmosphere_layer\" are used. The mass is the total mass of the molecules. The chemical formula for Halon1202 is CBr2F2. The IUPAC name for Halon1202 is dibromo(difluoro)methane."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CF12N48";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "atmosphere_mass_content_of_halon1202"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/KMP2/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/QHQLM3BE/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::QHQLM3BE";
        dc:date                "2018-04-16 15:20:49.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::QHQLM3BE";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-04-16 15:20:49.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/QHQLM3BE/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/stem_mass_content_of_carbon/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV16A67/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/stem_mass_content_of_carbon>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "\"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area. The stem of a plant is the axis that bears buds and shoots with leaves and, at its basal end, roots. Its function is to carry water and nutrients. Examples include the stalk of a plant or the main trunk of a tree."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::QHQLM3BE";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "stem_mass_content_of_carbon"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/KMP2/> .

