<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/S3BUHXH9/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::S3BUHXH9";
        dc:date                "2024-01-18 09:01:44.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::S3BUHXH9";
        pav:authoredOn         "2024-01-18 09:01:44.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/S3BUHXH9/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/difference_between_sea_surface_subskin_temperature_and_sea_surface_foundation_temperature/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/difference_between_sea_surface_subskin_temperature_and_sea_surface_foundation_temperature>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "This variable quantifies the temperature difference between the top (sea_surface_subskin_temperature) and bottom (sea_surface_foundation_temperature) of the diurnal warm layer. This diurnal warm layer, caused by absorption of solar radiation in the absence of strong mixing, together with a cool skin effect, account for the total temperature difference between the sea_surface_skin_temperature and the sea_surface_foundation_temperature. The cool skin effect is associated with the turbulent and infrared radiative heat loss at the air-sea interface. Freshwater fluxes may also affect this variable (sea_surface_subskin_temperature_minus_sea_surface_foundation_temperature)."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::S3BUHXH9";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "difference_between_sea_surface_subskin_temperature_and_sea_surface_foundation_temperature"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/UPAA/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/8QRKVDN5/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::8QRKVDN5";
        dc:date                "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::8QRKVDN5";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/8QRKVDN5/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/radioactivity_concentration_of_151Pm_in_air/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/radioactivity_concentration_of_151Pm_in_air>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "\"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Radioactivity concentration\" means radioactivity per unit volume of the medium. \"Pm\" means the element \"promethium\" and \"151Pm\" is the isotope \"promethium-151\" with a half-life of 1.18e+00 days."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::8QRKVDN5";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "radioactivity_concentration_of_151Pm_in_air"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/BQM3/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/B6RNUI5Q/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::B6RNUI5Q";
        dc:date                "2019-06-17 13:47:18.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::B6RNUI5Q";
        pav:authoredOn         "2019-06-17 13:47:18.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/B6RNUI5Q/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/mole_concentration_of_dissolved_molecular_nitrogen_in_sea_water/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/mole_concentration_of_dissolved_molecular_nitrogen_in_sea_water>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "\"Mole concentration\" means number of moles per unit volume, also called \"molarity\", and is used in the construction \"mole_concentration_of_X_in_Y\", where X is a material constituent of Y. A chemical or biological species denoted by X may be described by a single term such as \"nitrogen\" or a phrase such as \"nox_expressed_as_nitrogen\". The chemical formula for molecular nitrogen is N2."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::B6RNUI5Q";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "mole_concentration_of_dissolved_molecular_nitrogen_in_sea_water"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/MLM3/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/RQP10X4S/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::RQP10X4S";
        dc:date                "2024-05-20 20:39:49.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::RQP10X4S";
        pav:authoredOn         "2024-05-20 20:39:49.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/RQP10X4S/2/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/RQP10X4S/1/>;
        pav:version            "2";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/heat_index_of_air_temperature/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/heat_index_of_air_temperature>;
        owl:versionInfo        "2";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "Air temperature is the bulk temperature of the air, not the surface (skin) temperature. The quantity with standard name heat_index_of_air_temperature is the perceived air temperature when relative humidity is taken into consideration (which makes it feel hotter than the actual air temperature). Heat index is only defined when the ambient air temperature is at or above 299.817 K. References: https://www.weather.gov/safety/heat-index; WMO codes registry entry http://codes.wmo.int/grib2/codeflag/4.2/_0-0-12. It is strongly recommended that a variable with this standard name should have a units_metadata attribute, with one of the values \"on-scale\" or \"difference\", whichever is appropriate for the data, because it is essential to know whether the temperature is on-scale (meaning relative to the origin of the scale indicated by the units) or refers to temperature differences (implying that the origin of the temperature scale is irrevelant), in order to convert the units correctly (cf. https://cfconventions.org/cf-conventions/cf-conventions.html#temperature-units)."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::RQP10X4S";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "heat_index_of_air_temperature"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/UPKA/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/NYEJEW20/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::NYEJEW20";
        dc:date                "2017-06-26 15:24:29.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::NYEJEW20";
        pav:authoredOn         "2017-06-26 15:24:29.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/NYEJEW20/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/tendency_of_atmosphere_mass_content_of_reduced_nitrogen_compounds_expressed_as_nitrogen_due_to_dry_deposition/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/tendency_of_atmosphere_mass_content_of_reduced_nitrogen_compounds_expressed_as_nitrogen_due_to_dry_deposition>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "\"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area. The \"atmosphere content\" of a quantity refers to the vertical integral from the surface to the top of the atmosphere. For the content between specified levels in the atmosphere, standard names including \"content_of_atmosphere_layer\" are used. \"tendency_of_X\" means derivative of X with respect to time. The specification of a physical process by the phrase \"due_to_\" process means that the quantity named is a single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity named by omitting the phrase. \"Dry deposition\" is the sum of turbulent deposition and gravitational settling. \"Reduced nitrogen compounds\" means all chemical species containing nitrogen atoms with an oxidation state less than zero. Usually, particle bound and gaseous nitrogen compounds, primarily ammonium (NH4+) and ammonia (NH3), are included. The list of individual species that are included in this quantity can vary between models. Where possible, the data variable should be accompanied by a complete description of the species represented, for example, by using a comment attribute. The phrase \"expressed_as\" is used in the construction A_expressed_as_B, where B is a chemical constituent of A. It means that the quantity indicated by the standard name is calculated solely with respect to the B contained in A, neglecting all other chemical constituents of A."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::NYEJEW20";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "tendency_of_atmosphere_mass_content_of_reduced_nitrogen_compounds_expressed_as_nitrogen_due_to_dry_deposition"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/KSP2/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/A1E3PHJH/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::A1E3PHJH";
        dc:date                "2026-06-08 13:55:32.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::A1E3PHJH";
        pav:authoredOn         "2026-06-08 13:55:32.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/A1E3PHJH/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/ocean_number_content_of_mesopelagic_fish/>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "\"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area. Mesopelagic fish live in the mesopelagic or \"Twilight Zone\" at depths of about 200-1000 m, where light is limited."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::A1E3PHJH";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "ocean_number_content_of_mesopelagic_fish"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/PMSQ/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/YI375G77/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::YI375G77";
        dc:date                "2018-07-03 16:09:23.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::YI375G77";
        dc:replaces            <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0667/>;
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-07-03 16:09:23.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/YI375G77/2/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/YI375G77/1/>;
        pav:version            "2";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/downwelling_radiative_flux_per_unit_wavelength_in_air> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/downwelling_radiative_flux_per_unit_wavelength_in_air/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0667/>;
        owl:versionInfo        "2";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P02/current/VSRA/>;
        skos:definition        "Downwelling radiation is radiation from above. It does not mean \"net downward\". The sign convention is that \"upwelling\" is positive upwards and \"downwelling\" is positive downwards. When thought of as being incident on a surface, a radiative flux is sometimes called \"irradiance\". In addition, it is identical with the quantity measured by a cosine-collector light-meter and sometimes called \"vector irradiance\". In accordance with common usage in geophysical disciplines, \"flux\" implies per unit area, called \"flux density\" in physics. A coordinate variable for radiation wavelength should be given the standard name radiation_wavelength."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::YI375G77";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "downwelling_radiative_flux_per_unit_wavelength_in_air"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/WM2M/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0667/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CFSN0667";
        dc:date                "2013-06-27 14:07:56.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CFSN0667";
        dc:isReplacedBy        <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/YI375G77/>;
        pav:authoredOn         "2013-06-27 14:07:56.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0667/2/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0667/1/>;
        pav:version            "2";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "true";
        owl:sameAs             <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/downwelling_spectral_radiative_flux_in_air> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/downwelling_spectral_radiative_flux_in_air/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/YI375G77/>;
        owl:versionInfo        "2";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P04/current/G210/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P64/current/G210/>;
        skos:definition        "Downwelling radiation is radiation from above. It does not mean 'net downward'. 'spectral' means per unit wavelength or as a function of wavelength; spectral quantities are sometimes called 'monochromatic'. Radiation wavelength has standard name radiation_wavelength. When thought of as being incident on a surface, a radiative flux is sometimes called 'irradiance'. In addition, it is identical with the quantity measured by a cosine-collector light-meter and sometimes called 'vector irradiance'. In accordance with common usage in geophysical disciplines, 'flux' implies per unit area, called 'flux density' in physics."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CFSN0667";
        skos:note              "deprecated"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "downwelling_spectral_radiative_flux_in_air"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P02/current/VSRA/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/WM2M/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/P54AFUT9/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::P54AFUT9";
        dc:date                "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::P54AFUT9";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/P54AFUT9/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_131I_in_air/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_131I_in_air>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The phrase \"integral_wrt_X_of_Y\" means int Y dX. The data variable should have an axis for X specifying the limits of the integral as bounds. The phrase \"wrt\" means \"with respect to\". \"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Radioactivity concentration\" means radioactivity per unit volume of the medium. \"I\" means the element \"iodine\" and \"131I\" is the isotope \"iodine-131\" with a half-life of 8.07e+00 days."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::P54AFUT9";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_131I_in_air"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/BSM3/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0808/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CFSN0808";
        dc:date                "2009-07-06 16:30:45.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CFSN0808";
        dc:isReplacedBy        <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12S31/>;
        pav:authoredOn         "2009-07-06 16:30:45.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0808/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "true";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/mole_concentration_of_organic_detritus_in_sea_water_expressed_as_silicon/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12S31/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/mole_concentration_of_organic_detritus_in_sea_water_expressed_as_silicon>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "Mole concentration means moles (amount of substance) per unit volume and is used in the construction mole_concentration_of_X_in_Y, where X is a material constituent of Y.  The construction expressed_as_silicon means that the mole concentration is that of silicon atoms due to the organic detritus.  Organic detritus are particles of debris from decaying plants and animals."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CFSN0808";
        skos:note              "deprecated"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "mole_concentration_of_organic_detritus_in_sea_water_expressed_as_silicon"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/MLM3/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12S31/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CF12S31";
        dc:date                "2009-07-06 16:21:17.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CF12S31";
        dc:replaces            <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0808/>;
        pav:authoredOn         "2009-07-06 16:21:17.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12S31/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/mole_concentration_of_organic_detritus_expressed_as_silicon_in_sea_water> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/mole_concentration_of_organic_detritus_expressed_as_silicon_in_sea_water/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0808/>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P02/current/EXUV/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P64/current/G901/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P04/current/G901/>;
        skos:definition        "Mole concentration means number of moles per unit volume, also called \"molarity\", and is used in the construction mole_concentration_of_X_in_Y, where X is a material constituent of Y.  A chemical species denoted by X may be described by a single term such as 'nitrogen' or a phrase such as 'nox_expressed_as_nitrogen'. The phrase 'expressed_as' is used in the construction A_expressed_as_B, where B is a chemical constituent of A. It means that the quantity indicated by the standard name is calculated solely with respect to the B contained in A, neglecting all other chemical constituents of A. Organic detritus are particles of debris from decaying plants and animals."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CF12S31";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "mole_concentration_of_organic_detritus_expressed_as_silicon_in_sea_water"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/MLM3/> .

