        skos:definition        "The phrase \"integral_wrt_X_of_Y\" means int Y dX. The data variable should have an axis for X specifying the limits of the integral as bounds. The phrase \"wrt\" means \"with respect to\". \"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Radioactivity concentration\" means radioactivity per unit volume of the medium. \"Te\" means the element \"tellurium\" and \"131mTe\" is the metastable state of the isotope \"tellurium-131\" with a half-life of 1.25e+00 days."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::PL6PLX1R";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
