<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/HVC9X2PY/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::HVC9X2PY";
        dc:date                "2026-03-16 11:27:13.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::HVC9X2PY";
        pav:authoredOn         "2026-03-16 11:27:13.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/HVC9X2PY/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/photosynthesizing_vegetation_area_fraction/>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "Fraction of vegetation that is photosynthesizing (i.e. not dormant). Typically this will be green vegetation. Reference: Gutman & Ignatov, 1998 (https://doi.org/10.1080/014311698215333). \"Vegetation\" means any living plants e.g. trees, shrubs, grass. The term \"plants\" refers to the kingdom of plants in the modern classification which excludes fungi. Plants are autotrophs i.e. \"producers\" of biomass using carbon obtained from carbon dioxide. \"Area fraction\" is the fraction of a grid cell's horizontal area that has some characteristic of interest. It is evaluated as the area of interest divided by the grid cell area, or if the cell_methods restricts the evaluation to some portion of that grid cell (e.g. \"where sea_ice\"), then it is the area of interest divided by the area of the identified portion. It may be expressed as a fraction, a percentage, or any other dimensionless representation of a fraction."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::HVC9X2PY";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "photosynthesizing_vegetation_area_fraction"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/UUUU/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0311/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CFSN0311";
        dc:date                "2006-09-26 18:12:43.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CFSN0311";
        pav:authoredOn         "2006-09-26 18:12:43.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0311/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/specific_dry_energy_of_air/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/specific_dry_energy_of_air>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "'specific' means per unit mass. Dry energy is the sum of dry static energy and kinetic energy. Dry static energy is the sum of enthalpy and potential energy (itself the sum of gravitational and centripetal potential energy). Enthalpy can be written either as (1) CpT, where Cp is heat capacity at constant pressure, T is absolute temperature, or (2) U+pV, where U is internal energy, p is pressure and V is volume."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CFSN0311";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "specific_dry_energy_of_air"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/SQM2/> .

