        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P04/current/G540/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P02/current/IPHY/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P04/current/G644/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P64/current/G540/>;
        skos:definition        "\"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area. Thermal energy is the total vibrational energy, kinetic and potential, of all the molecules and atoms in a substance. Surface snow refers to the snow on the solid ground or on surface ice cover, but excludes, for example, falling snowflakes and snow on plants."@en;
