        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/tendency_of_atmosphere_moles_of_methyl_peroxy_radical/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/tendency_of_atmosphere_moles_of_methyl_peroxy_radical>;
        owl:versionInfo        "2";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The phrase \"tendency_of_X\" means derivative of X with respect to time. The construction \"atmosphere_moles_of_X\" means the total number of moles of X in the entire atmosphere, i.e. summed over the atmospheric column and over the entire globe. The chemical formula for methyl_peroxy_radical is CH3O2. In chemistry, a \"radical\" is a highly reactive, and therefore short lived, species."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CF12N725";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "tendency_of_atmosphere_moles_of_methyl_peroxy_radical"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/MLPS/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/7B360EMO/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::7B360EMO";
        dc:date                "2024-01-18 09:01:44.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::7B360EMO";
        pav:authoredOn         "2024-01-18 09:01:44.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/7B360EMO/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/mass_concentration_of_phosphorus_in_sea_floor_sediment/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/mass_concentration_of_phosphorus_in_sea_floor_sediment>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "\"Mass concentration\" means mass per unit volume and is used in the construction \"mass_concentration_of_X_in_Y\", where X is a material constituent of Y. A chemical species or biological group denoted by X may be described by a single term such as \"nitrogen\" or a phrase such as \"nox_expressed_as_nitrogen\". Phosphorus means phosphorus in all chemical forms, commonly referred to as \"total phosphorus\". \"Sea floor sediment\" is sediment deposited at the sea bed."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::7B360EMO";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "mass_concentration_of_phosphorus_in_sea_floor_sediment"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/UKMC/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0647/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CFSN0647";
        dc:date                "2006-09-26 18:12:43.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CFSN0647";
        pav:authoredOn         "2006-09-26 18:12:43.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0647/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/eastward_mass_flux_of_air/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/eastward_mass_flux_of_air>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "'Eastward' indicates a vector component which is positive when directed eastward (negative westward). In accordance with common usage in geophysical disciplines, 'flux' implies per unit area, called 'flux density' in physics."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CFSN0647";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "eastward_mass_flux_of_air"@en;
