        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The surface called \"surface\" means the lower boundary of the atmosphere. \"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area. \"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Tl\" means the element \"thallium\" and \"208Tl\" is the isotope \"thallium-208\" with a half-life of 2.15e-03 days."@en;
