        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/sea_surface_wave_maximum_crest_height/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/sea_surface_wave_maximum_crest_height>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The crest is the highest point of a wave. Crest height is the vertical distance between the crest and the calm sea surface. Maximum crest height is the maximum value measured during the observation period."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::UFJCG1TB";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "sea_surface_wave_maximum_crest_height"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/ULAA/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV16A42/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CFV16A42";
        dc:date                "2018-04-16 15:20:51.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CFV16A42";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-04-16 15:20:51.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV16A42/2/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV16A42/1/>;
        pav:version            "2";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "true";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/slow_soil_pool_carbon_content/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/I5DGQM0D/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/slow_soil_pool_carbon_content>;
        owl:versionInfo        "2";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "\"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area.  The \"soil content\" of a quantity refers to the vertical integral from the surface down to the bottom of the soil model. For the content between specified levels in the soil, standard names including content_of_soil_layer are used.  \"Soil carbon\" is the organic matter present in soil quantified by the mass of carbon it contains. Soil carbon is returned to the atmosphere as the organic matter decays. The decay process takes varying amounts of time depending on the composition of the organic matter, the temperature and the availability of moisture. A carbon \"soil pool\" means the carbon contained in organic matter which has a characteristic period over which it decays and releases carbon into the atmosphere. \"Slow soil pool\" refers to the decay of organic matter in soil with a characteristic period of more than a hundred years under reference climate conditions of a temperature of 20 degrees Celsius and no water limitations."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CFV16A42";
        skos:note              "deprecated"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "slow_soil_pool_carbon_content"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/KMP2/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/I5DGQM0D/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::I5DGQM0D";
        dc:date                "2018-04-16 15:20:49.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::I5DGQM0D";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-04-16 15:20:49.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/I5DGQM0D/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV16A42/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/slow_soil_pool_mass_content_of_carbon/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/slow_soil_pool_mass_content_of_carbon>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "\"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area. The \"soil content\" of a quantity refers to the vertical integral from the surface down to the bottom of the soil model. For the content between specified levels in the soil, standard names including content_of_soil_layer are used. Soil carbon is returned to the atmosphere as the organic matter decays. The decay process takes varying amounts of time depending on the composition of the organic matter, the temperature and the availability of moisture. A carbon \"soil pool\" means the carbon contained in organic matter which has a characteristic period over which it decays and releases carbon into the atmosphere. \"Slow soil pool\" refers to the decay of organic matter in soil with a characteristic period of more than a hundred years under reference climate conditions of a temperature of 20 degrees Celsius and no water limitations."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::I5DGQM0D";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "slow_soil_pool_mass_content_of_carbon"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/KMP2/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/S0TEUU6T/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::S0TEUU6T";
        dc:date                "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::S0TEUU6T";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/S0TEUU6T/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_147Pm_in_air/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_147Pm_in_air>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The phrase \"integral_wrt_X_of_Y\" means int Y dX. The data variable should have an axis for X specifying the limits of the integral as bounds. The phrase \"wrt\" means \"with respect to\". \"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Radioactivity concentration\" means radioactivity per unit volume of the medium. \"Pm\" means the element \"promethium\" and \"147Pm\" is the isotope \"promethium-147\" with a half-life of 9.57e+02 days."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::S0TEUU6T";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_147Pm_in_air"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/BSM3/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/Q41TRR91/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::Q41TRR91";
        dc:date                "2018-03-13 13:56:23.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::Q41TRR91";
