        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The surface called \"surface\" means the lower boundary of the atmosphere. \"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area. \"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Sb\" means the element \"antimony\" and \"125Sb\" is the isotope \"antimony-125\" with a half-life of 9.97e+02 days."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::0L7JO278";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "surface_radioactivity_content_of_125Sb"@en;
