        skos:definition        "The surface called \"surface\" means the lower boundary of the atmosphere. \"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area. \"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Gd\" means the element \"gadolinium\" and \"159Gd\" is the isotope \"gadolinium-159\" with a half-life of 7.71e-01 days."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::VP4DAED6";
