<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0218/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CFSN0218";
        dc:date                "2013-06-27 14:07:56.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CFSN0218";
        dc:isReplacedBy        <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CS10ZOYX/>;
        pav:authoredOn         "2013-06-27 14:07:56.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0218/2/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0218/1/>;
        pav:version            "2";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "true";
        owl:sameAs             <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/surface_upwelling_spectral_radiance_in_air> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CS10ZOYX/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/surface_upwelling_spectral_radiance_in_air/>;
        owl:versionInfo        "2";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The surface called 'surface' means the lower boundary of the atmosphere. Upwelling radiation is radiation from below. It does not mean 'net upward'. 'spectral' means per unit wavelength or as a function of wavelength; spectral quantities are sometimes called 'monochromatic'. Radiation wavelength has standard name radiation_wavelength. Radiance is the radiative flux in a particular direction, per unit of solid angle. The direction towards which it is going must be specified, for instance with a coordinate of zenith_angle. If the radiation does not depend on direction, a standard name of isotropic radiance should be chosen instead."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CFSN0218";
        skos:note              "deprecated"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "surface_upwelling_spectral_radiance_in_air"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P02/current/VSRA/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/WM2S/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CS10ZOYX/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CS10ZOYX";
        dc:date                "2018-07-03 16:09:23.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CS10ZOYX";
        dc:replaces            <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0218/>;
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-07-03 16:09:23.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CS10ZOYX/2/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CS10ZOYX/1/>;
        pav:version            "2";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/surface_upwelling_radiance_per_unit_wavelength_in_air> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/surface_upwelling_radiance_per_unit_wavelength_in_air/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0218/>;
        owl:versionInfo        "2";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P02/current/VSRW/>;
        skos:definition        "The surface called \"surface\" means the lower boundary of the atmosphere. Upwelling radiation is radiation from below. It does not mean \"net upward\". The sign convention is that \"upwelling\" is positive upwards and \"downwelling\" is positive downwards. Radiance is the radiative flux in a particular direction, per unit of solid angle. The direction towards which it is going must be specified, for instance with a coordinate of zenith_angle. If the radiation does not depend on direction, a standard name of isotropic radiance should be chosen instead. A coordinate variable for radiation wavelength should be given the standard name radiation_wavelength."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CS10ZOYX";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "surface_upwelling_radiance_per_unit_wavelength_in_air"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/WM2S/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/VQHW0V0R/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::VQHW0V0R";
        dc:date                "2026-09-15 05:36:53.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::VQHW0V0R";
        pav:authoredOn         "2026-09-15 05:36:53.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/VQHW0V0R/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/floating_ice_area_fraction/>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "\"Floating ice\" means all floating ice, including frozen sea water, frozen lake water, shelf ice, and calved land ice. \"Area fraction\" is the fraction of a grid cell's horizontal area that has some characteristic of interest. It is evaluated as the area of interest divided by the grid cell area, or if the cell_methods restricts the evaluation to some portion of that grid cell (e.g. \"where sea_ice\"), then it is the area of interest divided by the area of the identified portion. It may be expressed as a fraction, a percentage, or any other dimensionless representation of a fraction."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::VQHW0V0R";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "floating_ice_area_fraction"@en .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0696/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CFSN0696";
        dc:date                "2006-09-26 18:12:43.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CFSN0696";
        pav:authoredOn         "2006-09-26 18:12:43.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0696/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/downward_water_vapor_flux_in_air_due_to_diffusion/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/downward_water_vapor_flux_in_air_due_to_diffusion>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The specification of a physical process by the phrase due_to_process means that the quantity named is a single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity named by omitting the phrase. 'Downward' indicates a vector component which is positive when directed downward (negative upward). In accordance with common usage in geophysical disciplines, 'flux' implies per unit area, called 'flux density' in physics."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CFSN0696";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "downward_water_vapor_flux_in_air_due_to_diffusion"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/KSP2/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV8N36/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CFV8N36";
        dc:date                "2008-04-15 14:00:00.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CFV8N36";
        pav:authoredOn         "2008-04-15 14:00:00.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV8N36/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
