        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "\"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Radioactivity concentration\" means radioactivity per unit volume of the medium. \"Kr\" means the element \"krypton\" and \"89Kr\" is the isotope \"krypton-89\" with a half-life of 2.20e-03 days."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::ZD8P0PHB";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "radioactivity_concentration_of_89Kr_in_air"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/BQM3/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/QX7NSKA4/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::QX7NSKA4";
        dc:date                "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::QX7NSKA4";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/QX7NSKA4/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_127Sn_in_air/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_127Sn_in_air>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The phrase \"integral_wrt_X_of_Y\" means int Y dX. The data variable should have an axis for X specifying the limits of the integral as bounds. The phrase \"wrt\" means \"with respect to\". \"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Radioactivity concentration\" means radioactivity per unit volume of the medium. \"Sn\" means the element \"tin\" and \"127Sn\" is the isotope \"tin-127\" with a half-life of 8.84e-02 days."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::QX7NSKA4";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_127Sn_in_air"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/BSM3/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/60QCHKZK/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::60QCHKZK";
        dc:date                "2017-03-27 15:08:34.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::60QCHKZK";
        pav:authoredOn         "2017-03-27 15:08:34.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/60QCHKZK/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/sea_surface_primary_swell_wave_mean_period/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/sea_surface_primary_swell_wave_mean_period>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The quantity with standard name sea_surface_primary_swell_wave_mean_period is the mean period of the most energetic swell waves. Swell waves are waves on the ocean surface and are the low frequency portion of a bimodal wave frequency spectrum. The primary swell wave is the most energetic swell wave. A period is an interval of time, or the time-period of an oscillation. Wave period is the interval of time between repeated features on the waveform such as crests, troughs or upward passes through the mean level. Wave mean period is the mean period measured over the observation duration."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::60QCHKZK";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "sea_surface_primary_swell_wave_mean_period"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/UTBB/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSNA039/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CFSNA039";
        dc:date                "2006-09-26 18:12:43.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CFSNA039";
        dc:isReplacedBy        <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0217/>;
        pav:authoredOn         "2006-09-26 18:12:43.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSNA039/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "true";
        owl:sameAs             <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/surface_upwelling_shortwave_flux_assuming_clear_sky> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/surface_upwelling_shortwave_flux_assuming_clear_sky/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0217/>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P64/current/G210/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P64/current/G214/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P04/current/G214/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P02/current/CSLR/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P04/current/G210/>;
        skos:definition        "The surface called 'surface' means the lower boundary of the atmosphere. A phrase assuming_condition indicates that the named quantity is the value which would obtain if all aspects of the system were unaltered except for the assumption of the circumstances specified by the condition. 'shortwave' means shortwave radiation. Upwelling radiation is radiation from below. It does not mean 'net upward'. When thought of as being incident on a surface, a radiative flux is sometimes called 'irradiance'. In addition, it is identical with the quantity measured by a cosine-collector light-meter and sometimes called 'vector irradiance'. In accordance with common usage in geophysical disciplines, 'flux' implies per unit area, called 'flux density' in physics."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CFSNA039";
        skos:note              "deprecated"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "surface_upwelling_shortwave_flux_assuming_clear_sky"@en .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0217/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CFSN0217";
        dc:date                "2018-07-03 16:09:23.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CFSN0217";
        dc:replaces            <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSNA039/>;
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-07-03 16:09:23.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0217/2/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0217/1/>;
        pav:version            "2";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/surface_upwelling_shortwave_flux_in_air_assuming_clear_sky> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSNA039/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/surface_upwelling_shortwave_flux_in_air_assuming_clear_sky/>;
        owl:versionInfo        "2";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P64/current/G210/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P04/current/G210/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P64/current/G214/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P04/current/G214/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P02/current/CSLR/>;
        skos:definition        "The surface called \"surface\" means the lower boundary of the atmosphere. The term \"shortwave\" means shortwave radiation. Upwelling radiation is radiation from below. It does not mean \"net upward\". The sign convention is that \"upwelling\" is positive upwards and \"downwelling\" is positive downwards. When thought of as being incident on a surface, a radiative flux is sometimes called \"irradiance\". In addition, it is identical with the quantity measured by a cosine-collector light-meter and sometimes called \"vector irradiance\". In accordance with common usage in geophysical disciplines, \"flux\" implies per unit area, called \"flux density\" in physics. A phrase assuming_condition indicates that the named quantity is the value which would obtain if all aspects of the system were unaltered except for the assumption of the circumstances specified by the condition. \"Clear sky\" means in the absence of clouds."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CFSN0217";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "surface_upwelling_shortwave_flux_in_air_assuming_clear_sky"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/UFAA/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/ROMMVJ45/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::ROMMVJ45";
        dc:date                "2023-07-05 16:51:32.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::ROMMVJ45";
        pav:authoredOn         "2023-07-05 16:51:32.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/ROMMVJ45/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/mole_concentration_of_particulate_matter_expressed_as_calcium_in_sea_water/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/mole_concentration_of_particulate_matter_expressed_as_calcium_in_sea_water>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "\"Mole concentration\" means number of moles per unit volume, also called \"molarity\", and is used in the construction \"mole_concentration_of_X_in_Y\", where X is a material constituent of Y. A chemical species or biological group denoted by X may be described by a single term such as \"nitrogen\" or a phrase such as \"nox_expressed_as_nitrogen\". The phrase \"expressed_as\" is used in the construction \"A_expressed_as_B\", where B is a chemical constituent of A. It means that the quantity indicated by the standard name is calculated solely with respect to the B contained in A, neglecting all other chemical constituents of A. Particulate means suspended solids of all sizes."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::ROMMVJ45";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "mole_concentration_of_particulate_matter_expressed_as_calcium_in_sea_water"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/MLM3/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV16A36/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CFV16A36";
        dc:date                "2018-07-03 16:09:23.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CFV16A36";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-07-03 16:09:23.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV16A36/3/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV16A36/1/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV16A36/2/>;
        pav:version            "3";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/sea_ice_salinity> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/sea_ice_salinity/>;
        owl:versionInfo        "3";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P02/current/ICHM/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P02/current/IPHY/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P25/current/ICESSALIN/>;
        skos:definition        "Sea ice salinity is the salt content of sea ice, often on the Practical Salinity Scale of 1978. However, the unqualified term 'salinity' is generic and does not necessarily imply any particular method of calculation. The units of salinity are dimensionless and normally given as 1e-3 or 0.001 i.e. parts per thousand. Practical Salinity is reported on the Practical Salinity Scale of 1978 (PSS-78), and is usually based on the electrical conductivity of sea water in observations since the 1960s. \"Sea ice\" means all ice floating in the sea which has formed from freezing sea water, rather than by other processes such as calving of land ice to form icebergs."@en;
        skos:inScheme          <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/scheme/NETOC_PARAM/current/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/scheme/NETMAR_OCEAN/current/>;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CFV16A36";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "sea_ice_salinity"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/UUUU/> .

