        owl:versionInfo        "2";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "\"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area. The \"atmosphere content\" of a quantity refers to the vertical integral from the surface to the top of the atmosphere. For the content between specified levels in the atmosphere, standard names including \"content_of_atmosphere_layer\" are used. The mass is the total mass of the particles.  \"Aerosol\" means the system of suspended liquid or solid particles in air (except cloud droplets) and their carrier gas, the air itself. Aerosol particles take up ambient water (a process known as hygroscopic growth) depending on the relative humidity and the composition of the particles. \"Dry aerosol particles\" means aerosol particles without any water uptake. The specification of a physical process by the phrase \"due_to_\" process means that the quantity named is a single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity named by omitting the phrase. \"Emission\" means emission from a primary source located anywhere within the atmosphere, including at the lower boundary (i.e. the surface of the earth). \"Emission\" is a process entirely distinct from \"re-emission\" which is used in some standard names. \"tendency_of_X\" means derivative of X with respect to time."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::8FKHOJ0X";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "tendency_of_atmosphere_mass_content_of_dust_dry_aerosol_particles_due_to_emission"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/KSP2/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N122/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CF12N122";
        dc:date                "2009-07-06 15:41:29.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CF12N122";
        pav:authoredOn         "2009-07-06 15:41:29.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N122/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/atmosphere_moles_of_bromine_monoxide/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/atmosphere_moles_of_bromine_monoxide>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P02/current/HLAT/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P04/current/G142/>;
        skos:definition        "The construction \"atmosphere_moles_of_X\" means the total number of moles of X in the entire atmosphere, i.e. summed over the atmospheric column and over the entire globe. The chemical formula for bromine monoxide is BrO."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CF12N122";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "atmosphere_moles_of_bromine_monoxide"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/MOLE/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV16A59/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CFV16A59";
        dc:date                "2018-07-03 16:09:23.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CFV16A59";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-07-03 16:09:23.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV16A59/2/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV16A59/1/>;
        pav:version            "2";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/tendency_of_sea_ice_amount_due_to_congelation_ice_accumulation/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/tendency_of_sea_ice_amount_due_to_congelation_ice_accumulation>;
        owl:versionInfo        "2";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P02/current/CRYS/>;
        skos:definition        "The phrase \"tendency_of_X\" means derivative of X with respect to time. \"Amount\" means mass per unit area. \"Sea ice\" means all ice floating in the sea which has formed from freezing sea water, rather than by other processes such as calving of land ice to form icebergs. The specification of a physical process by the phrase due_to_process means that the quantity named is a single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity named by omitting the phrase. \"Congelation ice\" means the freezing of sea water onto the underside of thin, new sea ice that has been formed by small areas of frazil ice crystals joining together into a continuous layer at the sea surface. Congelation ice forms under calm water conditions; it thickens and stabilizes the layer of sea ice and produces a smooth bottom surface."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CFV16A59";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "tendency_of_sea_ice_amount_due_to_congelation_ice_accumulation"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/KSP2/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/JTRYEUMI/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::JTRYEUMI";
        dc:date                "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::JTRYEUMI";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/JTRYEUMI/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_151Nd_in_air/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_151Nd_in_air>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The phrase \"integral_wrt_X_of_Y\" means int Y dX. The data variable should have an axis for X specifying the limits of the integral as bounds. The phrase \"wrt\" means \"with respect to\". \"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Radioactivity concentration\" means radioactivity per unit volume of the medium. \"Nd\" means the element \"neodymium\" and \"151Nd\" is the isotope \"neodymium-151\" with a half-life of 8.61e-03 days."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::JTRYEUMI";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_151Nd_in_air"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/BSM3/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/WO8GKMFX/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::WO8GKMFX";
        dc:date                "2023-04-24 17:39:19.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::WO8GKMFX";
        pav:authoredOn         "2023-04-24 17:39:19.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/WO8GKMFX/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/soil_water_salinity/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/soil_water_salinity>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "soil_water_salinity is the salt content of soil water, often on the Practical Salinity Scale of 1978. However, the unqualified term 'salinity' is generic and does not necessarily imply any particular method of calculation. The units of salinity are dimensionless and normally given as 1e-3 or 0.001 i.e. parts per thousand."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::WO8GKMFX";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "soil_water_salinity"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/UUUU/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0490/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CFSN0490";
        dc:date                "2018-02-12 16:53:19.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CFSN0490";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-02-12 16:53:19.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0490/2/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0490/1/>;
        pav:version            "2";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/northward_ocean_salt_transport_due_to_diffusion> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/northward_ocean_salt_transport_due_to_diffusion/>;
        owl:versionInfo        "2";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P04/current/G996/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P64/current/G996/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P02/current/VDFC/>;
        skos:definition        "\"Northward\" indicates a vector component which is positive when directed northward (negative southward). \"Salt transport\" means the mass of salt being transported. Northward transport by diffusion means the part due to horizontal or isopyncal diffusion schemes in an ocean model, but not including the parameterized eddy velocity. The specification of a physical process by the phrase due_to_process means that the quantity named is a single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity named by omitting the phrase."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CFSN0490";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "northward_ocean_salt_transport_due_to_diffusion"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/KGPS/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/6WRVG0ER/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::6WRVG0ER";
        dc:date                "2026-06-08 13:55:32.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::6WRVG0ER";
        pav:authoredOn         "2026-06-08 13:55:32.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/6WRVG0ER/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/ocean_number_content_of_demersal_fish/>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "\"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area. Demersal fish spend a fraction of their lives in close association with the seabed, feeding primarily on bottom organisms, they can carry out diel vertical migrations (e.g. cod)."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::6WRVG0ER";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "ocean_number_content_of_demersal_fish"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/PMSQ/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0147/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CFSN0147";
        dc:date                "2006-09-26 18:12:43.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CFSN0147";
        pav:authoredOn         "2006-09-26 18:12:43.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0147/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/tendency_of_northward_wind_due_to_diffusion> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/tendency_of_northward_wind_due_to_diffusion/>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P02/current/EWSB/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P64/current/G259/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P04/current/G259/>;
        skos:definition        "The specification of a physical process by the phrase due_to_process means that the quantity named is a single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity named by omitting the phrase. 'tendency_of_X' means derivative of X with respect to time. 'Northward' indicates a vector component which is positive when directed northward (negative southward). Wind is defined as a two-dimensional (horizontal) air velocity vector, with no vertical component. (Vertical motion in the atmosphere has the standard name upward_air_velocity.)"@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CFSN0147";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "tendency_of_northward_wind_due_to_diffusion"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/MPS2/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/XDOLIOAF/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::XDOLIOAF";
        dc:date                "2022-03-18 12:42:55.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::XDOLIOAF";
        pav:authoredOn         "2022-03-18 12:42:55.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/XDOLIOAF/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/mass_concentration_of_19_butanoyloxyfucoxanthin_in_sea_water/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/mass_concentration_of_19_butanoyloxyfucoxanthin_in_sea_water>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "\"Mass concentration\" means mass per unit volume and is used in the construction \"mass_concentration_of_X_in_Y\", where X is a material constituent of Y. A chemical species or biological group denoted by X may be described by a single term such as \"nitrogen\" or a phrase such as \"nox_expressed_as_nitrogen\". The chemical formula of 19'-butanoyloxyfucoxanthin is C46H64O8. The equivalent term in the NERC P01 Parameter Usage Vocabulary may be found at http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P01/current/BUTAXXXX/1/."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::XDOLIOAF";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "mass_concentration_of_19_butanoyloxyfucoxanthin_in_sea_water"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/UKMC/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/2GH3EG3F/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::2GH3EG3F";
        dc:date                "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::2GH3EG3F";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/2GH3EG3F/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/radioactivity_concentration_of_148Pm_in_air/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/radioactivity_concentration_of_148Pm_in_air>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "\"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Radioactivity concentration\" means radioactivity per unit volume of the medium. \"Pm\" means the element \"promethium\" and \"148Pm\" is the isotope \"promethium-148\" with a half-life of 5.38e+00 days."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::2GH3EG3F";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "radioactivity_concentration_of_148Pm_in_air"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/BQM3/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV13N8/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CFV13N8";
        dc:date                "2018-07-03 16:09:23.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CFV13N8";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-07-03 16:09:23.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV13N8/2/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV13N8/1/>;
        pav:version            "2";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/downwelling_shortwave_flux_in_air_assuming_clear_sky/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/downwelling_shortwave_flux_in_air_assuming_clear_sky>;
        owl:versionInfo        "2";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P02/current/VSRA/>;
        skos:definition        "Downwelling radiation is radiation from above. It does not mean \"net downward\". The sign convention is that \"upwelling\" is positive upwards and \"downwelling\" is positive downwards. The term \"shortwave\" means shortwave radiation. When thought of as being incident on a surface, a radiative flux is sometimes called \"irradiance\". In addition, it is identical with the quantity measured by a cosine-collector light-meter and sometimes called \"vector irradiance\". In accordance with common usage in geophysical disciplines, \"flux\" implies per unit area, called \"flux density\" in physics. A phrase assuming_condition indicates that the named quantity is the value which would obtain if all aspects of the system were unaltered except for the assumption of the circumstances specified by the condition. \"Clear sky\" means in the absence of clouds."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CFV13N8";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "downwelling_shortwave_flux_in_air_assuming_clear_sky"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/UFAA/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0720/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CFSN0720";
        dc:date                "2006-09-26 18:12:43.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CFSN0720";
        pav:authoredOn         "2006-09-26 18:12:43.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0720/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/coriolis_parameter/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/coriolis_parameter>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P02/current/CHUM/>;
        skos:definition        "The Coriolis parameter is twice the component of the earth's angular velocity about the local vertical i.e. 2 W sin L, where L is latitude and W the angular speed of the earth."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CFSN0720";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "coriolis_parameter"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/PRSC/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N278/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CF12N278";
