        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The surface called \"surface\" means the lower boundary of the atmosphere. \"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area. \"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Zn\" means the element \"zinc\" and \"72Zn\" is the isotope \"zinc-72\" with a half-life of 1.94e+00 days."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::874Y3LT7";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "surface_radioactivity_content_of_72Zn"@en;
