        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/atmosphere_moles_of_ethanol/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/atmosphere_moles_of_ethanol>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The construction \"atmosphere_moles_of_X\" means the total number of moles of X in the entire atmosphere, i.e. summed over the atmospheric column and over the entire globe. The chemical formula for ethanol is C2H5OH."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CF12N136";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "atmosphere_moles_of_ethanol"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/MOLE/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/1P00IASX/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::1P00IASX";
        dc:date                "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::1P00IASX";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/1P00IASX/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_129I_in_air/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_129I_in_air>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The phrase \"integral_wrt_X_of_Y\" means int Y dX. The data variable should have an axis for X specifying the limits of the integral as bounds. The phrase \"wrt\" means \"with respect to\". \"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Radioactivity concentration\" means radioactivity per unit volume of the medium. \"I\" means the element \"iodine\" and \"129I\" is the isotope \"iodine-129\" with a half-life of 5.81e+09 days."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::1P00IASX";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_129I_in_air"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/BSM3/> .

