        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The surface called \"surface\" means the lower boundary of the atmosphere. \"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area. \"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Cs\" means the element \"cesium\" and \"135mCs\" is the metastable state of the isotope \"cesium-135\" with a half-life of 3.68e-02 days."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::N5S4NYBR";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "surface_radioactivity_content_of_135mCs"@en;
