        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The surface called \"surface\" means the lower boundary of the atmosphere. \"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area. \"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"U\" means the element \"uranium\" and \"232U\" is the isotope \"uranium-232\" with a half-life of 2.63e+04 days."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::JWQBZPI1";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "surface_radioactivity_content_of_232U"@en;
