<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0179/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CFSN0179";
        dc:date                "2006-09-26 18:12:43.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CFSN0179";
        pav:authoredOn         "2006-09-26 18:12:43.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0179/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/tendency_of_dry_energy_content_of_atmosphere_layer/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/tendency_of_dry_energy_content_of_atmosphere_layer>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "'tendency_of_X' means derivative of X with respect to time. 'Content' indicates a quantity per unit area. 'Layer' means any layer with upper and lower boundaries that have constant values in some vertical coordinate. There must be a vertical coordinate variable indicating the extent of the layer(s). If the layers are model layers, the vertical coordinate can be model_level_number, but it is recommended to specify a physical coordinate (in a scalar or auxiliary coordinate variable) as well. Dry energy is the sum of dry static energy and kinetic energy. Dry static energy is the sum of enthalpy and potential energy (itself the sum of gravitational and centripetal potential energy). Enthalpy can be written either as (1) CpT, where Cp is heat capacity at constant pressure, T is absolute temperature, or (2) U+pV, where U is internal energy, p is pressure and V is volume."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CFSN0179";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "tendency_of_dry_energy_content_of_atmosphere_layer"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/UFAA/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/J2ZAL3RP/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::J2ZAL3RP";
        dc:date                "2015-07-08 15:41:36.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::J2ZAL3RP";
        pav:authoredOn         "2015-07-08 15:41:36.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/J2ZAL3RP/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/cloud_binary_mask/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/cloud_binary_mask>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "X_binary_mask has 1 where condition X is met, 0 elsewhere. 1 = cloud present, 0 = cloud absent (clear). If no threshold is supplied, the binary mask is 1 if there is any non-zero amount of cloud. if a threshold is supplied, it should be specified by associating a coordinate variable or scalar coordinate variable with the data variable and giving the coordinate variable a standard name of cloud_area_fraction. The values of the coordinate variable are the threshold values for the corresponding subarrays of the data variable."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::J2ZAL3RP";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "cloud_binary_mask"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/UUUU/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N80/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CF12N80";
        dc:date                "2009-07-06 15:41:29.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CF12N80";
