        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/surface_snow_mass/>;
        owl:versionInfo        "2";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "Surface snow refers to the amount on the solid ground or on surface ice cover, but excludes, for example, falling snowflakes and snow on plants. The horizontal domain over which surface snow mass is calculated is described by the associated coordinate variables and coordinate bounds or by a coordinate variable or scalar coordinate variable with the standard name of \"region\" supplied according to section 6.1.1 of the CF conventions."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::D5YTQY3B";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "surface_snow_mass"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/KGXX/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/XTO8ZRGA/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::XTO8ZRGA";
        dc:date                "2019-12-09 17:20:23.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::XTO8ZRGA";
        pav:authoredOn         "2019-12-09 17:20:23.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/XTO8ZRGA/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/sea_surface_wave_stokes_drift_speed/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/sea_surface_wave_stokes_drift_speed>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The Stokes drift velocity is the average velocity when following a specific fluid parcel as it travels with the fluid flow. For instance, a particle floating at the free surface of water waves, experiences a net Stokes drift velocity in the direction of wave propagation. Speed is the magnitude of velocity."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::XTO8ZRGA";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "sea_surface_wave_stokes_drift_speed"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/UVAA/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/1QGXY8WK/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::1QGXY8WK";
        dc:date                "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::1QGXY8WK";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/1QGXY8WK/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_13N_in_air/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_13N_in_air>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The phrase \"integral_wrt_X_of_Y\" means int Y dX. The data variable should have an axis for X specifying the limits of the integral as bounds. The phrase \"wrt\" means \"with respect to\". \"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Radioactivity concentration\" means radioactivity per unit volume of the medium. \"N\" means the element \"nitrogen\" and \"13N\" is the isotope \"nitrogen-13\" with a half-life of 6.92e-03 days."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::1QGXY8WK";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_13N_in_air"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/BSM3/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N624/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CF12N624";
        dc:date                "2009-07-06 15:41:29.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CF12N624";
        pav:authoredOn         "2009-07-06 15:41:29.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N624/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/tendency_of_atmosphere_mass_content_of_ethyne_due_to_emission> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/tendency_of_atmosphere_mass_content_of_ethyne_due_to_emission/>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P04/current/G140/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P02/current/AEYN/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P02/current/ATEM/>;
        skos:definition        "\"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area.  The \"atmosphere content\" of a quantity refers to the vertical integral from the surface to the top of the atmosphere. For the content between specified levels in the atmosphere, standard names including content_of_atmosphere_layer are used.  The specification of a physical process by the phrase due_to_process means that the quantity named is a  single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity  named by omitting the phrase.  \"tendency_of_X\" means derivative of X with respect to time.  \"Emission\" means emission from a primary source located anywhere within the atmosphere, including at the lower boundary (i.e. earth's surface). \"Emission\" is a process entirely distinct from \"re-emission\" which is used in some standard names. The chemical formula for ethyne is HC2H.  Ethyne is the IUPAC name for this species, which is also commonly known as acetylene."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CF12N624";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "tendency_of_atmosphere_mass_content_of_ethyne_due_to_emission"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/KSP2/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0510/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CFSN0510";
        dc:date                "2018-02-12 16:53:19.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CFSN0510";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-02-12 16:53:19.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0510/2/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0510/1/>;
        pav:version            "2";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/northward_ocean_freshwater_transport_due_to_gyre> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/northward_ocean_freshwater_transport_due_to_gyre/>;
        owl:versionInfo        "2";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P02/current/VDFC/>;
        skos:definition        "\"Northward\" indicates a vector component which is positive when directed northward (negative southward). Northward transport by the ocean gyre is geometrically defined as being the part due to the vertical integral of the product of deviations of velocity and tracer from their zonal means. The velocity does not include the parameterized eddy velocity. The specification of a physical process by the phrase due_to_process means that the quantity named is a single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity named by omitting the phrase."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CFSN0510";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "northward_ocean_freshwater_transport_due_to_gyre"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P04/current/G917/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/KGPS/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P64/current/G917/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N134/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CF12N134";
