        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The surface called \"surface\" means the lower boundary of the atmosphere. \"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area. \"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Ba\" means the element \"barium\" and \"140Ba\" is the isotope \"barium-140\" with a half-life of 1.28e+01 days."@en;
