        pav:authoredOn         "2019-06-17 13:47:19.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/X62TUKSM/2/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/X62TUKSM/1/>;
        pav:version            "2";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "true";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/I6891JNB/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/TOGASZOW/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/tendency_of_sea_water_salinity_expressed_as_salt_content_due_to_parameterized_eddy_dianeutral_mixing/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/tendency_of_sea_water_salinity_expressed_as_salt_content_due_to_parameterized_eddy_dianeutral_mixing>;
        owl:versionInfo        "2";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The phrase \"tendency_of_X\" means derivative of X with respect to time. \"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area. The specification of a physical process by the phrase due_to_process means that the quantity named is a single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity named by omitting the phrase. \"Eddy dianeutral mixing\" means dianeutral mixing, i.e. mixing across neutral directions caused by the unresolved turbulent motion of eddies of all types (e.g., breaking gravity waves, boundary layer turbulence, etc.)."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::X62TUKSM";
        skos:note              "deprecated"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "tendency_of_sea_water_salinity_expressed_as_salt_content_due_to_parameterized_eddy_dianeutral_mixing"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/KSP2/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/TOGASZOW/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::TOGASZOW";
        dc:date                "2025-03-19 08:31:35.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::TOGASZOW";
        pav:authoredOn         "2025-03-19 08:31:35.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/TOGASZOW/2/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/TOGASZOW/1/>;
        pav:version            "2";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "true";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/I6891JNB/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/X62TUKSM/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/tendency_of_sea_water_salinity_expressed_as_salt_content_due_to_parameterized_dianeutral_mixing/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/tendency_of_sea_water_salinity_expressed_as_salt_content_due_to_parameterized_dianeutral_mixing>;
        owl:versionInfo        "2";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The phrase \"tendency_of_X\" means derivative of X with respect to time. \"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area. The specification of a physical process by the phrase due_to_process means that the quantity named is a single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity named by omitting the phrase. \"Dianeutral mixing\" means mixing across surfaces of neutral buoyancy. \"Parameterized\" means the part due to a scheme representing processes which are not explicitly resolved by the model."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::TOGASZOW";
        skos:note              "deprecated"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "tendency_of_sea_water_salinity_expressed_as_salt_content_due_to_parameterized_dianeutral_mixing"@en;
