        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "\"Turbulent mixing length\" is used in models to describe the average distance over which a fluid parcel can travel while retaining properties that allow the parcel to be distinguished from its immediate environment. \"Turbulent mixing\" means chaotic fluctuations of the fluid flow."@en;
