        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/radioactivity_concentration_of_222Rn_in_air/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/radioactivity_concentration_of_222Rn_in_air>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "\"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Radioactivity concentration\" means radioactivity per unit volume of the medium. \"Rn\" means the element \"radon\" and \"222Rn\" is the isotope \"radon-222\" with a half-life of 3.82e+00 days."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::BPGHUBBG";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "radioactivity_concentration_of_222Rn_in_air"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/BQM3/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0330/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CFSN0330";
        dc:date                "2013-03-23 09:23:01.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CFSN0330";
        pav:authoredOn         "2013-03-23 09:23:01.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0330/3/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0330/1/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0330/2/>;
        pav:version            "3";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/sea_water_pressure> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/sea_water_pressure/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P04/current/G958/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P64/current/G958/>;
        owl:versionInfo        "3";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P04/current/G667/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P02/current/AHGT/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P02/current/PREX/>;
        skos:definition        "\"Sea water pressure\" is the pressure that exists in the medium of sea water.  It includes the pressure due to overlying sea water, sea ice, air and any other medium that may be present. For sea water pressure excluding the pressure due to overlying media other than sea water, the standard name sea_water_pressure_due_to_sea_water should be used."@en;
        skos:narrower          <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P01/current/PRESPR01/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P04/current/G957/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P64/current/G957/>;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CFSN0330";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "sea_water_pressure"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/UPDB/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/4FVAJL2E/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::4FVAJL2E";
        dc:date                "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::4FVAJL2E";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/4FVAJL2E/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_139Ba_in_air/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_139Ba_in_air>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The phrase \"integral_wrt_X_of_Y\" means int Y dX. The data variable should have an axis for X specifying the limits of the integral as bounds. The phrase \"wrt\" means \"with respect to\". \"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Radioactivity concentration\" means radioactivity per unit volume of the medium. \"Ba\" means the element \"barium\" and \"139Ba\" is the isotope \"barium-139\" with a half-life of 5.77e-02 days."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::4FVAJL2E";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_139Ba_in_air"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/BSM3/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/3MFK5ESJ/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::3MFK5ESJ";
        dc:date                "2026-09-15 05:36:52.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::3MFK5ESJ";
        pav:authoredOn         "2026-09-15 05:36:52.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/3MFK5ESJ/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/probability_of_mass_concentration_of_volcanic_ash_in_air_at_or_above_threshold/>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "\"probability_of_X_at_or_above_threshold\" means the chance that X is at or above the threshold. Space and time coordinates must be used to indicate the area and time to which a probability applies. \"Mass concentration\" means mass per unit volume and is used in the construction \"mass_concentration_of_X_in_Y\", where X is a material constituent of Y. A chemical species or biological group denoted by X may be described by a single term such as \"nitrogen\" or a phrase such as \"nox_expressed_as_nitrogen\". \"Volcanic ash\" means the fine-grained products of explosive volcanic eruptions, such as minerals or crystals, older fragmented rock (e.g. andesite) and glass. Particles within a volcanic ash cloud have diameters less than 2 mm. \"Volcanic ash\" does not include non-volcanic dust. It must have a coordinate variable or scalar coordinate variable with the standard name of mass_concentration_of_volcanic_ash_in_air to supply the threshold(s)."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::3MFK5ESJ";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "probability_of_mass_concentration_of_volcanic_ash_in_air_at_or_above_threshold"@en .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0369/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
