        skos:definition        "The surface called \"surface\" means the lower boundary of the atmosphere. \"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area. \"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Tb\" means the element \"terbium\" and \"160Tb\" is the isotope \"terbium-160\" with a half-life of 7.23e+01 days."@en;
