        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/surface_radioactivity_content_of_232Pa/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/surface_radioactivity_content_of_232Pa>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The surface called \"surface\" means the lower boundary of the atmosphere. \"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area. \"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Pa\" means the element \"protactinium\" and \"232Pa\" is the isotope \"protactinium-232\" with a half-life of 1.31e+00 days."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::0R0JQ51G";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "surface_radioactivity_content_of_232Pa"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/BQSM/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0287/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CFSN0287";
        dc:date                "2018-07-03 16:09:23.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CFSN0287";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-07-03 16:09:23.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0287/3/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0287/1/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0287/2/>;
        pav:version            "3";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/surface_downwelling_photosynthetic_photon_spherical_irradiance_in_sea_water> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/surface_downwelling_photosynthetic_photon_spherical_irradiance_in_sea_water/>;
        owl:versionInfo        "3";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P64/current/G950/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P64/current/G947/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P02/current/VSRW/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P04/current/G950/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P04/current/G947/>;
        skos:definition        "The surface called \"surface\" means the lower boundary of the atmosphere. Downwelling radiation is radiation from above. It does not mean \"net downward\". The sign convention is that \"upwelling\" is positive upwards and \"downwelling\" is positive downwards. \"Photosynthetic\" radiation is the part of the spectrum which is used in photosynthesis e.g. 400-700 nm. The range of wavelengths could be specified precisely by the bounds of a coordinate of radiation_wavelength. Photon spherical irradiance is the photon flux incident on unit area of a hemispherical (or \"2-pi\") collector. The direction (\"up/downwelling\") is specified. Radiation incident on a 4-pi collector has standard names of \"omnidirectional spherical irradiance\". A photon flux is specified in terms of numbers of photons expressed in moles."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CFSN0287";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "surface_downwelling_photosynthetic_photon_spherical_irradiance_in_sea_water"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/M2MS/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N44/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CF12N44";
        dc:date                "2009-07-06 15:41:29.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CF12N44";
        pav:authoredOn         "2009-07-06 15:41:29.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N44/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/atmosphere_mass_content_of_formaldehyde/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/atmosphere_mass_content_of_formaldehyde>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P04/current/G135/>;
        skos:definition        "\"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area.  The \"atmosphere content\" of a quantity refers to the vertical integral from the surface to the top of the atmosphere. For the content between specified levels in the atmosphere, standard names including content_of_atmosphere_layer are used.  The chemical formula for formaldehyde is CH2O. The IUPAC name for formaldehyde is methanal."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CF12N44";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "atmosphere_mass_content_of_formaldehyde"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/KMP2/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/J95ROWAH/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::J95ROWAH";
        dc:date                "2018-05-29 16:57:01.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::J95ROWAH";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-05-29 16:57:01.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/J95ROWAH/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/frequency_of_lightning_flashes_per_unit_area/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/frequency_of_lightning_flashes_per_unit_area>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "A lightning flash is a compound event, usually consisting of several discharges. Frequency is the number of oscillations of a wave, or the number of occurrences of an event, per unit time."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::J95ROWAH";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "frequency_of_lightning_flashes_per_unit_area"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/M2S2/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/7HBAHG55/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::7HBAHG55";
        dc:date                "2018-05-15 09:59:16.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::7HBAHG55";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-05-15 09:59:16.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/7HBAHG55/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/mass_flux_of_nitrogen_compounds_expressed_as_nitrogen_out_of_litter_and_soil_due_to_immobilisation_and_remineralization/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/mass_flux_of_nitrogen_compounds_expressed_as_nitrogen_out_of_litter_and_soil_due_to_immobilisation_and_remineralization>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "In accordance with common usage in geophysical disciplines, \"flux\" implies per unit area, called \"flux density\" in physics. The phrase \"expressed_as\" is used in the construction A_expressed_as_B, where B is a chemical constituent of A. It means that the quantity indicated by the standard name is calculated solely with respect to the B contained in A, neglecting all other chemical constituents of A. \"Nitrogen compounds\" summarizes all chemical species containing nitrogen atoms. \"Litter\" is dead plant material in or above the soil. It is distinct from coarse wood debris. The precise distinction between \"fine\" and \"coarse\" is model dependent. The specification of a physical process by the phrase \"due_to_\" process means that the quantity named is a single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity named by omitting the phrase. Remineralization is the degradation of organic matter into inorganic forms of carbon, nitrogen, phosphorus and other micronutrients, which consumes oxygen and releases energy. Immobilisation of nitrogen refers to retention of nitrogen by micro-organisms under certain conditions, making it unavailable for plants."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::7HBAHG55";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "mass_flux_of_nitrogen_compounds_expressed_as_nitrogen_out_of_litter_and_soil_due_to_immobilisation_and_remineralization"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/KSP2/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0570/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CFSN0570";
        dc:date                "2006-09-26 18:12:43.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CFSN0570";
        pav:authoredOn         "2006-09-26 18:12:43.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0570/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/lwe_thickness_of_snowfall_amount> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/lwe_thickness_of_snowfall_amount/>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P64/current/G284/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P64/current/G290/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P04/current/G290/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P02/current/CPRP/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P04/current/G285/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P64/current/G285/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P04/current/G284/>;
        skos:definition        "'lwe' means liquid water equivalent. 'Amount' means mass per unit area. The construction lwe_thickness_of_X_amount or _content means the vertical extent of a layer of liquid water having the same mass per unit area."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CFSN0570";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "lwe_thickness_of_snowfall_amount"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/ULAA/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/Q3H382LX/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::Q3H382LX";
        dc:date                "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::Q3H382LX";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/Q3H382LX/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/surface_radioactivity_content_of_101Mo/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/surface_radioactivity_content_of_101Mo>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The surface called \"surface\" means the lower boundary of the atmosphere. \"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area. \"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Mo\" means the element \"molybdenum\" and \"101Mo\" is the isotope \"molybdenum-101\" with a half-life of 1.01e-02 days."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::Q3H382LX";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "surface_radioactivity_content_of_101Mo"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/BQSM/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0496/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CFSN0496";
        dc:date                "2006-09-26 18:12:43.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CFSN0496";
        pav:authoredOn         "2006-09-26 18:12:43.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0496/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/net_rate_of_absorption_of_shortwave_energy_in_atmosphere_layer> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/net_rate_of_absorption_of_shortwave_energy_in_atmosphere_layer/>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P64/current/G214/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P04/current/G214/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P04/current/G197/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P64/current/G197/>;
        skos:definition        "'shortwave' means shortwave radiation. 'Layer' means any layer with upper and lower boundaries that have constant values in some vertical coordinate. There must be a vertical coordinate variable indicating the extent of the layer(s). If the layers are model layers, the vertical coordinate can be model_level_number, but it is recommended to specify a physical coordinate (in a scalar or auxiliary coordinate variable) as well. Net absorbed radiation is the difference between absorbed and emitted radiation."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CFSN0496";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "net_rate_of_absorption_of_shortwave_energy_in_atmosphere_layer"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/UFAA/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N45/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CFV10N45";
        dc:date                "2008-10-21 10:00:00.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CFV10N45";
        pav:authoredOn         "2008-10-21 10:00:00.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N45/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/tendency_of_potential_energy_content_of_ocean_layer_due_to_diffusion/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/tendency_of_potential_energy_content_of_ocean_layer_due_to_diffusion>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The specification of a physical process by the phrase due_to_process means that the quantity named is a single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity named by omitting the phrase. \"tendency_of_X\" means derivative of X with respect to time. \"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area. \"Layer\" means any layer with upper and lower boundaries that have constant values in some vertical coordinate. There must be a vertical coordinate variable indicating the extent of the layer(s). If the layers are model layers, the vertical coordinate can be model_level_number, but it is recommended to specify a physical coordinate (in a scalar or auxiliary coordinate variable) as well. Potential energy is the sum of the gravitational potential energy relative to the geoid and the centripetal potential energy. (The geopotential is the specific potential energy.)"@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CFV10N45";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "tendency_of_potential_energy_content_of_ocean_layer_due_to_diffusion"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/UFAA/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/DOBETSX5/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::DOBETSX5";
        dc:date                "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::DOBETSX5";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/DOBETSX5/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_87Kr_in_air/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_87Kr_in_air>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The phrase \"integral_wrt_X_of_Y\" means int Y dX. The data variable should have an axis for X specifying the limits of the integral as bounds. The phrase \"wrt\" means \"with respect to\". \"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Radioactivity concentration\" means radioactivity per unit volume of the medium. \"Kr\" means the element \"krypton\" and \"87Kr\" is the isotope \"krypton-87\" with a half-life of 5.28e-02 days."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::DOBETSX5";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_87Kr_in_air"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/BSM3/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/NK7W2T5M/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::NK7W2T5M";
