<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/WRYHHEE2/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::WRYHHEE2";
        dc:date                "2024-01-18 09:01:44.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::WRYHHEE2";
        pav:authoredOn         "2024-01-18 09:01:44.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/WRYHHEE2/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/integral_wrt_height_of_product_of_eastward_wind_and_mass_concentration_of_water_vapor_in_air/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/integral_wrt_height_of_product_of_eastward_wind_and_mass_concentration_of_water_vapor_in_air>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "Eastward vertically-integrated moisture flux per unit length in latitude. \"Eastward\" indicates a vector component which is positive when directed eastward (negative westward). Height is the vertical distance above the surface. Wind is defined as a two-dimensional (horizontal) air velocity vector, with no vertical component. (Vertical motion in the atmosphere has the standard name \"upward_air_velocity\"). The phrase \"product_of_X_and_Y\" means X*Y. The abbreviation \"wrt\" means \"with respect to\". The phrase \"integral_wrt_X_of_Y\" means int Y dX. To specify the limits of the integral the data variable should have an axis for X and associated coordinate bounds. If no axis for X is associated with the data variable, or no coordinate bounds are specified, it is assumed that the integral is calculated over the entire vertical extent of the medium, e.g, if the medium is air the integral is assumed to be calculated over the full depth of the atmosphere. \"Mass concentration\" means mass per unit volume and is used in the construction \"mass_concentration_of_X_in_Y\", where X is a material constituent of Y. A chemical species or biological group denoted by X may be described by a single term such as \"nitrogen\" or a phrase such as \"nox_expressed_as_nitrogen\"."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::WRYHHEE2";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "integral_wrt_height_of_product_of_eastward_wind_and_mass_concentration_of_water_vapor_in_air"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/KMPS/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/U2HD33ZJ/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::U2HD33ZJ";
        dc:date                "2017-02-21 16:02:00.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::U2HD33ZJ";
        pav:authoredOn         "2017-02-21 16:02:00.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/U2HD33ZJ/2/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/U2HD33ZJ/1/>;
        pav:version            "2";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "true";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/B58LZ0OO/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/floating_ice_sheet_area_fraction/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/floating_ice_sheet_area_fraction>;
        owl:versionInfo        "2";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "\"X_area_fraction\" means the fraction of horizontal area occupied by X. A \"floating ice sheet\", sometimes called an \"ice shelf\", indicates where the ice sheet is flowing over sea water."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::U2HD33ZJ";
        skos:note              "deprecated"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "floating_ice_sheet_area_fraction"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/UUUU/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/B58LZ0OO/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::B58LZ0OO";
        dc:date                "2024-09-04 12:51:23.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::B58LZ0OO";
        pav:authoredOn         "2024-09-04 12:51:23.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/B58LZ0OO/3/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/B58LZ0OO/2/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/B58LZ0OO/1/>;
        pav:version            "3";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/floating_ice_shelf_area_fraction/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/floating_ice_shelf_area_fraction> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/U2HD33ZJ/>;
        owl:versionInfo        "3";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "\"Area fraction\" is the fraction of a grid cell's horizontal area that has some characteristic of interest. It is evaluated as the area of interest divided by the grid cell area, or if the cell_methods restricts the evaluation to some portion of that grid cell (e.g. \"where sea_ice\"), then it is the area of interest divided by the area of the identified portion. It may be expressed as a fraction, a percentage, or any other dimensionless representation of a fraction. A \"floating ice shelf\", sometimes called a \"floating ice sheet\", indicates where an ice sheet extending from a land area flows over sea water."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::B58LZ0OO";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "floating_ice_shelf_area_fraction"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/UUUU/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/EFCTNKNQ/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::EFCTNKNQ";
        dc:date                "2022-03-18 12:42:55.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::EFCTNKNQ";
        pav:authoredOn         "2022-03-18 12:42:55.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/EFCTNKNQ/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/mass_concentration_of_chlorophyll_c3_in_sea_water/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/mass_concentration_of_chlorophyll_c3_in_sea_water>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "\"Mass concentration\" means mass per unit volume and is used in the construction \"mass_concentration_of_X_in_Y\", where X is a material constituent of Y. A chemical species or biological group denoted by X may be described by a single term such as \"nitrogen\" or a phrase such as \"nox_expressed_as_nitrogen\". Chlorophylls are the green pigments found in most plants, algae and cyanobacteria; their presence is essential for photosynthesis to take place. There are several different forms of chlorophyll that occur naturally. All contain a chlorin ring (chemical formula C20H16N4) which gives the green pigment and a side chain whose structure varies. The naturally occurring forms of chlorophyll contain between 35 and 55 carbon atoms. The chemical formula of chlorophyll c3 is C36H44MgN4O7. The equivalent term in the NERC P01 Parameter Usage Vocabulary may be found at http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P01/current/CHLC03PX/2/."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::EFCTNKNQ";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "mass_concentration_of_chlorophyll_c3_in_sea_water"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/UKMC/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV15A14/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CFV15A14";
        dc:date                "2018-08-06 12:15:46.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CFV15A14";
        dc:replaces            <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0593/>;
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-08-06 12:15:46.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV15A14/2/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV15A14/1/>;
        pav:version            "2";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0593/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/stratiform_precipitation_amount> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/stratiform_precipitation_amount/>;
        owl:versionInfo        "2";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P02/current/CPRP/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P04/current/G285/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P64/current/G285/>;
        skos:definition        "\"Precipitation\" in the earth's atmosphere means precipitation of water in all phases. Stratiform precipitation, whether liquid or frozen, is precipitation that formed in stratiform cloud. \"Amount\" means mass per unit area."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CFV15A14";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "stratiform_precipitation_amount"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/KMP2/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0593/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CFSN0593";
        dc:date                "2010-07-26 09:53:35.0";
